I go to work by bus. I start work at nine. At twelve, I eat lunch with my friends. I finish work at five.

In the evening, I cook dinner. After dinner, I read a book or watch TV. I go to bed at eleven.', 70, 28, '[{"lemma":"breakfast","pos":"noun","meaning_tr":"kahvaltı","example":"Breakfast is at seven.","example_tr":"Kahvaltı yedide."},{"lemma":"lunch","pos":"noun","meaning_tr":"öğle yemeği","example":"We have lunch at noon.","example_tr":"Öğlen yemek yeriz."},{"lemma":"dinner","pos":"noun","meaning_tr":"akşam yemeği","example":"I cook dinner at six.","example_tr":"Altıda akşam yemeği pişiririm."},{"lemma":"finish","pos":"verb","meaning_tr":"bitirmek","example":"I finish work at five.","example_tr":"İşi beşte bitiririm.","forms":["finishes","finished"]}]'::jsonb, '[{"prompt":"What does Lena drink at breakfast?","options":["Coffee","Tea","Milk","Juice"],"answer":1},{"prompt":"How does she go to work?","options":["By bus","By car","On foot","By bike"],"answer":0},{"prompt":"When does she go to bed?","options":["At nine","At ten","At eleven","At twelve"],"answer":2}]'::jsonb, 'DilYolu özgün içerik', 'Kişisel kullanım') on conflict (language_code, slug) do update set title = excluded.title, kind = excluded.kind, cefr_level = excluded.cefr_level, topics = excluded.topics, body = excluded.body, word_count = excluded.word_count, est_read_sec = excluded.est_read_sec, glossary = excluded.glossary, questions = excluded.questions;

On Saturday, we visited the castle, which stands on a hill in the middle of the city. The view was fantastic, but it was very windy! In the afternoon, we walked along the Royal Mile and bought some small presents for our families.

On Sunday, it rained, so we went to a museum and had lunch in a traditional pub. I tried haggis for the first time. It was better than I expected. We came home tired, but we both want to go back soon.', 116, 46, '[{"lemma":"castle","pos":"noun","meaning_tr":"kale","example":"The castle is very old.","example_tr":"Kale çok eski."},{"lemma":"view","pos":"noun","meaning_tr":"manzara","example":"The view from the hill is great.","example_tr":"Tepeden manzara harika."},{"lemma":"windy","pos":"adj","meaning_tr":"rüzgârlı","example":"It is windy today.","example_tr":"Bugün hava rüzgârlı."},{"lemma":"present","pos":"noun","meaning_tr":"hediye","example":"I bought a present for my sister.","example_tr":"Kız kardeşime hediye aldım.","forms":["presents"]},{"lemma":"expect","pos":"verb","meaning_tr":"beklemek, tahmin etmek","example":"I didn''t expect so many people.","example_tr":"Bu kadar çok insan beklemiyordum.","forms":["expected","expects"]}]'::jsonb, '[{"prompt":"How did they travel to Edinburgh?","options":["By plane","By car","By train","By bus"],"answer":2},{"prompt":"What was the weather like on Saturday?","options":["Rainy","Very windy","Snowy","Hot"],"answer":1,"explain_tr":"“It was very windy!”"},{"prompt":"Why did they go to a museum on Sunday?","options":["It was free","It was raining","They were bored","A friend worked there"],"answer":1},{"prompt":"What does the writer think about haggis?","options":["It was terrible","It was better than expected","It was too expensive","They didn''t try it"],"answer":1}]'::jsonb, 'DilYolu özgün içerik', 'Kişisel kullanım') on conflict (language_code, slug) do update set title = excluded.title, kind = excluded.kind, cefr_level = excluded.cefr_level, topics = excluded.topics, body = excluded.body, word_count = excluded.word_count, est_read_sec = excluded.est_read_sec, glossary = excluded.glossary, questions = excluded.questions;

However, remote work is not without problems. Some employees report feeling isolated, because they rarely meet colleagues in person. Others find it difficult to separate work from private life, especially when their desk is in the living room.

As a result, many companies are now trying a hybrid model, in which staff work from home on some days and come to the office on others. Supporters say this combines the advantages of both worlds, although critics point out that it requires careful planning to work well.', 134, 54, '[{"lemma":"privilege","pos":"noun","meaning_tr":"ayrıcalık","example":"Education is a privilege for some.","example_tr":"Eğitim bazıları için bir ayrıcalıktır."},{"lemma":"appreciate","pos":"verb","meaning_tr":"takdir etmek, değer vermek","example":"I appreciate your help.","example_tr":"Yardımını takdir ediyorum.","forms":["appreciated","appreciates"]},{"lemma":"isolated","pos":"adj","meaning_tr":"yalnızlaşmış, izole","example":"He felt isolated in the new city.","example_tr":"Yeni şehirde kendini yalnız hissetti."},{"lemma":"hybrid","pos":"adj","meaning_tr":"karma, hibrit","example":"A hybrid car uses two kinds of energy.","example_tr":"Hibrit araba iki tür enerji kullanır."},{"lemma":"advantage","pos":"noun","meaning_tr":"avantaj","example":"Speaking two languages is an advantage.","example_tr":"İki dil bilmek bir avantajdır.","forms":["advantages"]}]'::jsonb, '[{"prompt":"Why do workers appreciate working from home?","options":["They earn more","They save time and money on travel","They have shorter days","They get free equipment"],"answer":1},{"prompt":"Which problem is mentioned?","options":["Slow internet","Feeling isolated","Lack of computers","High rent"],"answer":1},{"prompt":"What is a hybrid model?","options":["Working only in the office","Working only at home","Working at home on some days and in the office on others","Working at night"],"answer":2},{"prompt":"What do critics say about the hybrid model?","options":["It is too cheap","It needs careful planning","It never works","It is illegal"],"answer":1}]'::jsonb, 'DilYolu özgün içerik', 'Kişisel kullanım') on conflict (language_code, slug) do update set title = excluded.title, kind = excluded.kind, cefr_level = excluded.cefr_level, topics = excluded.topics, body = excluded.body, word_count = excluded.word_count, est_read_sec = excluded.est_read_sec, glossary = excluded.glossary, questions = excluded.questions;

The consequences of chronic sleep deprivation are well documented. People who regularly sleep fewer than six hours are more likely to suffer from heart disease, to gain weight and to have difficulty concentrating. Perhaps more surprisingly, even a single poor night can impair judgement to a degree comparable with mild intoxication.

Experts therefore recommend keeping regular hours, avoiding screens before bed and limiting caffeine in the afternoon. Such measures sound unremarkable, but, when followed consistently, they can make a considerable difference to both health and productivity.', 134, 54, '[{"lemma":"tempting","pos":"adj","meaning_tr":"cazip, caydırıcı","example":"The offer is tempting.","example_tr":"Teklif cazip.","forms":["tempted"]},{"lemma":"adequate","pos":"adj","meaning_tr":"yeterli","example":"We have adequate food for everyone.","example_tr":"Herkes için yeterli yiyeceğimiz var."},{"lemma":"consolidate","pos":"verb","meaning_tr":"pekiştirmek","example":"Sleep helps consolidate memories.","example_tr":"Uyku anıları pekiştirmeye yardımcı olur.","forms":["consolidates","consolidated"]},{"lemma":"chronic","pos":"adj","meaning_tr":"kronik","example":"She suffers from chronic back pain.","example_tr":"Kronik sırt ağrısı çekiyor."},{"lemma":"impair","pos":"verb","meaning_tr":"bozmak, zayıflatmak","example":"Noise can impair concentration.","example_tr":"Gürültü konsantrasyonu bozabilir.","forms":["impairs","impaired"]}]'::jsonb, '[{"prompt":"What does the first paragraph say sleep does for the brain?","options":["Makes it grow","Stores memories and restores emotional balance","Speeds up reaction times","Replaces eating"],"answer":1},{"prompt":"According to the text, what can a single bad night do?","options":["Cure heart disease","Impair judgement","Improve memory","Increase appetite only"],"answer":1},{"prompt":"Which advice is NOT mentioned?","options":["Keep regular hours","Avoid screens before bed","Limit afternoon caffeine","Exercise every morning"],"answer":3,"explain_tr":"Sabah egzersizi metinde geçmiyor."}]'::jsonb, 'DilYolu özgün içerik', 'Kişisel kullanım') on conflict (language_code, slug) do update set title = excluded.title, kind = excluded.kind, cefr_level = excluded.cefr_level, topics = excluded.topics, body = excluded.body, word_count = excluded.word_count, est_read_sec = excluded.est_read_sec, glossary = excluded.glossary, questions = excluded.questions;

This does not mean that progress should be leisurely for its own sake. Rather, it suggests that struggle is not a sign of failure but a condition of genuine learning. Learners who tolerate confusion, revisit difficult material and allow time between sessions tend to retain more, even if they feel less confident in the short term.

The implication is uncomfortable but liberating: there are no shortcuts, yet there is no need to panic either. Steady, deliberate practice, sustained over months, will outperform any frantic burst of effort.', 152, 61, '[{"lemma":"prize","pos":"verb","meaning_tr":"çok değer vermek","example":"She prizes honesty above all.","example_tr":"Dürüstlüğe her şeyden çok değer verir.","forms":["prizes"]},{"lemma":"perverse","pos":"adj","meaning_tr":"ters, mantıksız","example":"It seems perverse to refuse help.","example_tr":"Yardımı reddetmek mantıksız görünüyor."},{"lemma":"cram","pos":"verb","meaning_tr":"ezberlemek (son anda), tıkıştırmak","example":"He crammed all night.","example_tr":"Bütün gece ezberledi.","forms":["crammed"]},{"lemma":"tolerate","pos":"verb","meaning_tr":"tahammül etmek, hoş görmek","example":"I can’t tolerate noise.","example_tr":"Gürültüye tahammül edemem."},{"lemma":"liberating","pos":"adj","meaning_tr":"özgürleştirici","example":"Quitting was liberating.","example_tr":"Bırakmak özgürleştiriciydi."}]'::jsonb, '[{"prompt":"What is the author’s main argument?","options":["Speed is the key to learning","Durable learning requires spaced, effortful practice","Language apps are useless","Examinations should be abolished"],"answer":1},{"prompt":"According to the text, what is struggle?","options":["A sign of failure","A condition of genuine learning","A waste of time","Only a problem for beginners"],"answer":1},{"prompt":"What does the author find “uncomfortable but liberating”?","options":["That learning can be fast","That there are no shortcuts, but no need to panic","That apps are expensive","That memory is unreliable"],"answer":1}]'::jsonb, 'DilYolu özgün içerik', 'Kişisel kullanım') on conflict (language_code, slug) do update set title = excluded.title, kind = excluded.kind, cefr_level = excluded.cefr_level, topics = excluded.topics, body = excluded.body, word_count = excluded.word_count, est_read_sec = excluded.est_read_sec, glossary = excluded.glossary, questions = excluded.questions;

Now I play for my family on Sundays. My little sister sings, and my parents clap. I am not a great guitarist yet, but I enjoy it more than anything else. Next month, I am going to join a small music class at the community centre.', 100, 40, '[{"lemma":"hobby","pos":"noun","meaning_tr":"hobi","example":"Reading is my favourite hobby.","example_tr":"Okumak en sevdiğim hobi."},{"lemma":"practise","pos":"verb","meaning_tr":"pratik yapmak, çalışmak","example":"You must practise every day.","example_tr":"Her gün pratik yapmalısın.","forms":["practised"]},{"lemma":"simple","pos":"adj","meaning_tr":"basit","example":"This is a simple recipe.","example_tr":"Bu basit bir tarif."},{"lemma":"clap","pos":"verb","meaning_tr":"alkışlamak","example":"The audience clapped loudly.","example_tr":"Seyirci yüksek sesle alkışladı."},{"lemma":"community centre","pos":"noun","meaning_tr":"mahalle merkezi","example":"The class is at the community centre.","example_tr":"Ders mahalle merkezinde."}]'::jsonb, '[{"prompt":"Who taught the writer to play the guitar?","options":["Her sister","Julia","A music teacher"],"answer":1},{"prompt":"How long did the writer practise each evening?","options":["Ten minutes","Twenty minutes","One hour"],"answer":1},{"prompt":"What is the writer going to do next month?","options":["Buy a new guitar","Join a music class","Move to a new city"],"answer":1}]'::jsonb, 'DilYolu özgün içerik', 'Kişisel kullanım') on conflict (language_code, slug) do update set title = excluded.title, kind = excluded.kind, cefr_level = excluded.cefr_level, topics = excluded.topics, body = excluded.body, word_count = excluded.word_count, est_read_sec = excluded.est_read_sec, glossary = excluded.glossary, questions = excluded.questions;

However, working from home is not perfect. Some people feel isolated and miss the conversations they used to have with colleagues. Others find it hard to separate work from private life, so they end up working longer hours than before. Managers also worry that it is more difficult to train new employees online.

Many firms are now trying a compromise: two or three days in the office and the rest at home. Most workers seem to prefer this balance, although it depends on the job and the person.', 149, 60, '[{"lemma":"commute","pos":"verb","meaning_tr":"işe gidip gelmek","example":"I commute by train every day.","example_tr":"Her gün trenle işe gidip geliyorum."},{"lemma":"concentrate","pos":"verb","meaning_tr":"odaklanmak","example":"I cannot concentrate with this noise.","example_tr":"Bu gürültüyle odaklanamıyorum."},{"lemma":"isolated","pos":"adj","meaning_tr":"yalnız, izole","example":"She felt isolated in the new city.","example_tr":"Yeni şehirde kendini yalnız hissetti."},{"lemma":"compromise","pos":"noun","meaning_tr":"orta yol, uzlaşma","example":"We reached a compromise.","example_tr":"Bir orta yol bulduk."},{"lemma":"employee","pos":"noun","meaning_tr":"çalışan","example":"The company has fifty employees.","example_tr":"Şirketin elli çalışanı var.","forms":["employees"]}]'::jsonb, '[{"prompt":"What is one advantage for employees?","options":["They earn more money","They save commuting time and money","They have more meetings"],"answer":1},{"prompt":"What problem do some people have at home?","options":["The internet is too slow","They work longer hours","They sleep too much"],"answer":1},{"prompt":"What compromise do many firms try?","options":["Only working from home","Two or three days in the office","Shorter working weeks"],"answer":1}]'::jsonb, 'DilYolu özgün içerik', 'Kişisel kullanım') on conflict (language_code, slug) do update set title = excluded.title, kind = excluded.kind, cefr_level = excluded.cefr_level, topics = excluded.topics, body = excluded.body, word_count = excluded.word_count, est_read_sec = excluded.est_read_sec, glossary = excluded.glossary, questions = excluded.questions;

Critics point out that this abundance has a downside. Faced with endless choice, many viewers spend more time browsing than watching. Moreover, because platforms rely on subscriptions, they compete fiercely for attention, and some producers feel pressure to deliver an exciting opening rather than a carefully developed plot.

Streaming has also altered the economics of the industry. While it has opened doors for international productions that would once have been ignored, it has made it harder for smaller studios to earn a fair share of the profits. Whether the model is sustainable remains an open question.', 165, 66, '[{"lemma":"abundance","pos":"noun","meaning_tr":"bolluk","example":"There is an abundance of food.","example_tr":"Bol miktarda yiyecek var."},{"lemma":"downside","pos":"noun","meaning_tr":"olumsuz yan, dezavantaj","example":"The downside is the high price.","example_tr":"Olumsuz yanı yüksek fiyat."},{"lemma":"subscription","pos":"noun","meaning_tr":"abonelik","example":"I cancelled my subscription.","example_tr":"Aboneliğimi iptal ettim.","forms":["subscriptions"]},{"lemma":"fiercely","pos":"adv","meaning_tr":"şiddetle, sert biçimde","example":"The two teams competed fiercely.","example_tr":"İki takım sert biçimde yarıştı."},{"lemma":"sustainable","pos":"adj","meaning_tr":"sürdürülebilir","example":"We need a sustainable solution.","example_tr":"Sürdürülebilir bir çözüme ihtiyacımız var."}]'::jsonb, '[{"prompt":"How has streaming changed the way series are released?","options":["One episode a month","Whole series at once","Only at weekends"],"answer":1},{"prompt":"What downside do critics mention?","options":["Too few titles","Viewers spend a lot of time browsing","Prices are too low"],"answer":1},{"prompt":"Why can smaller studios struggle?","options":["They produce too much","It is harder to earn a fair share of profits","They refuse to use streaming"],"answer":1}]'::jsonb, 'DilYolu özgün içerik', 'Kişisel kullanım') on conflict (language_code, slug) do update set title = excluded.title, kind = excluded.kind, cefr_level = excluded.cefr_level, topics = excluded.topics, body = excluded.body, word_count = excluded.word_count, est_read_sec = excluded.est_read_sec, glossary = excluded.glossary, questions = excluded.questions;

The explanation lies partly in the burden of decision-making. When alternatives proliferate, each rejected option becomes a potential source of regret, and the chooser is left with an unsettling sense that a better outcome was within reach. Paradoxically, the person who has chosen from the largest menu may end up the least satisfied.

This does not imply that choice is inherently harmful. Rather, it suggests that satisfaction depends on how we choose. People who set clear criteria in advance, and who are content with a result that is good enough, tend to report greater well-being than those who relentlessly pursue the optimal.', 170, 68, '[{"lemma":"assumption","pos":"noun","meaning_tr":"varsayım","example":"The theory rests on a false assumption.","example_tr":"Teori yanlış bir varsayıma dayanıyor."},{"lemma":"bewildering","pos":"adj","meaning_tr":"şaşırtıcı, kafa karıştırıcı","example":"The menu offered a bewildering choice.","example_tr":"Menü kafa karıştırıcı bir seçenek sunuyordu."},{"lemma":"proliferate","pos":"verb","meaning_tr":"çoğalmak","example":"Mobile apps have proliferated.","example_tr":"Mobil uygulamalar çoğaldı.","forms":["proliferate"]},{"lemma":"unsettling","pos":"adj","meaning_tr":"huzursuz edici","example":"It was an unsettling silence.","example_tr":"Huzursuz edici bir sessizlikti."},{"lemma":"relentlessly","pos":"adv","meaning_tr":"amansızca, durmaksızın","example":"He worked relentlessly on the project.","example_tr":"Proje üzerinde durmaksızın çalıştı."}]'::jsonb, '[{"prompt":"What did the jam experiment show?","options":["Shoppers prefer larger selections","Shoppers with fewer choices bought more","Price decided everything"],"answer":1},{"prompt":"Why might people with the most options be less satisfied?","options":["They always choose cheaply","Rejected options become sources of regret","They dislike shopping"],"answer":1},{"prompt":"What helps satisfaction according to the text?","options":["Setting clear criteria and accepting good enough","Always seeking the optimal","Avoiding all choices"],"answer":0}]'::jsonb, 'DilYolu özgün içerik', 'Kişisel kullanım') on conflict (language_code, slug) do update set title = excluded.title, kind = excluded.kind, cefr_level = excluded.cefr_level, topics = excluded.topics, body = excluded.body, word_count = excluded.word_count, est_read_sec = excluded.est_read_sec, glossary = excluded.glossary, questions = excluded.questions;

I hope you are well. I was wondering if you are free on Saturday evening. I''m planning a small dinner at my place at seven o''clock, and I would love to see you. Would you like to come? I will cook a Turkish dish that I think you will like.

Let me know if you can make it.

Best wishes,
Ali', ARRAY['günlük hayat', 'yemek']::text[]) on conflict (language_code, slug) do update set cefr_level = excluded.cefr_level, kind = excluded.kind, title_tr = excluded.title_tr, prompt_tr = excluded.prompt_tr, target_phrases = excluded.target_phrases, min_words = excluded.min_words, max_words = excluded.max_words, sample_answer = excluded.sample_answer, topics = excluded.topics;
• I → am
• he / she / it → is
• we / you / they → are

Olumsuz için fiilden sonra not eklenir: I am not, he is not (isn''t), they are not (aren''t). Soru için fiil özneden önce gelir: Are you ready?', '[{"text":"I am a teacher.","tr":"Ben öğretmenim.","highlight":"am"},{"text":"She is from Italy.","tr":"O İtalya''lıdır.","highlight":"is"},{"text":"They are not at home.","tr":"Onlar evde değil.","highlight":"are not"},{"text":"Are you hungry?","tr":"Aç mısın?","highlight":"Are"}]'::jsonb, '[{"type":"mcq","prompt":"He ___ my brother.","options":["am","is","are","be"],"answer":1,"explain_tr":"he/she/it ile “is” kullanılır."},{"type":"mcq","prompt":"We ___ in the kitchen.","options":["is","am","are","be"],"answer":2},{"type":"fill","prompt":"I ___ tired today. (am/is/are)","answer":"am"},{"type":"fill","prompt":"___ they your friends? (Am/Is/Are)","answer":"are","explain_tr":"Soruda fiil başa gelir; they ile “are”."},{"type":"mcq","prompt":"Which sentence is correct?","options":["She are happy.","She is happy.","She am happy.","She be happy."],"answer":1}]'::jsonb, 1) on conflict (language_code, slug) do update set title_tr = excluded.title_tr, title_target = excluded.title_target, cefr_level = excluded.cefr_level, summary_tr = excluded.summary_tr, examples = excluded.examples, practice_items = excluded.practice_items, order_index = excluded.order_index;
• a / an → belirsiz, tek bir şey (“bir”). Sesli harfle başlayan sözcüklerde “an”: an apple, an hour. Diğerlerinde “a”: a book.
• the → belirli, hem konuşan hem dinleyen hangisinden söz edildiğini biliyor: the sun, the book on the table.
• İlk kez söz edince a/an, tekrar söz edince the: I have a dog. The dog is big.
• Çoğul ve sayılamayan isimlerde genel anlatımda artikel kullanılmaz: I like music.', '[{"text":"I have a cat and an umbrella.","tr":"Bir kedim ve bir şemsiyem var.","highlight":"a cat and an umbrella"},{"text":"The cat is under the table.","tr":"Kedi masanın altında.","highlight":"The cat"},{"text":"She is an engineer.","tr":"O bir mühendis.","highlight":"an engineer"},{"text":"I like coffee.","tr":"Kahveyi severim.","highlight":"coffee"}]'::jsonb, '[{"type":"mcq","prompt":"She eats ___ apple every day.","options":["a","an","the","one"],"answer":1,"explain_tr":"“apple” sesli harfle başladığı için “an” gelir."},{"type":"mcq","prompt":"I saw a film yesterday. ___ film was great.","options":["A","An","The","Some"],"answer":2,"explain_tr":"Film daha önce söz edildiği için belirli: the."},{"type":"fill","prompt":"He is ___ honest man. (a/an)","answer":"an","explain_tr":"“honest” sesli harfle (h okunmaz) başlar; an honest man."},{"type":"mcq","prompt":"Which sentence is correct?","options":["I need an umbrella.","I need a umbrella.","I need the umbrellas a.","I need umbrella."],"answer":0},{"type":"fill","prompt":"Open ___ window, please. (a/an/the)","answer":"the","explain_tr":"Hangi pencere olduğu belli olduğunda “the” kullanılır."}]'::jsonb, 2) on conflict (language_code, slug) do update set title_tr = excluded.title_tr, title_target = excluded.title_target, cefr_level = excluded.cefr_level, summary_tr = excluded.summary_tr, examples = excluded.examples, practice_items = excluded.practice_items, order_index = excluded.order_index;
• Olumlu: I/you/we/they + fiil; he/she/it + fiil+s → She works.
• Olumsuz: don’t / doesn’t + fiilin yalın hâli → He doesn’t work. (works değil!)
• Soru: Do / Does + özne + yalın fiil → Does she work here?
• Sık kullanılan zarflar: always, usually, often, sometimes, never; fiilden önce, “be”den sonra gelir.', '[{"text":"I drink tea every morning.","tr":"Her sabah çay içerim.","highlight":"drink"},{"text":"She works in a bank.","tr":"O bir bankada çalışıyor.","highlight":"works"},{"text":"He doesn’t like fish.","tr":"Balığı sevmez.","highlight":"doesn’t like"},{"text":"Do you speak English?","tr":"İngilizce konuşuyor musun?","highlight":"Do you speak"}]'::jsonb, '[{"type":"mcq","prompt":"My brother ___ football on Sundays.","options":["play","plays","playing","is play"],"answer":1,"explain_tr":"he/she/it ile fiile -s eklenir."},{"type":"mcq","prompt":"She ___ coffee. She prefers tea.","options":["don’t drink","doesn’t drinks","doesn’t drink","isn’t drink"],"answer":2,"explain_tr":"doesn’t’ten sonra fiil yalın kalır."},{"type":"fill","prompt":"___ they live in London? (Do/Does)","answer":"Do","explain_tr":"they ile Do kullanılır."},{"type":"fill","prompt":"He ___ up at six. (get)","answer":"gets","explain_tr":"he ile -s: gets."},{"type":"mcq","prompt":"Which sentence is correct?","options":["Does he works here?","Does he work here?","Do he work here?","He does work here?"],"answer":1}]'::jsonb, 3) on conflict (language_code, slug) do update set title_tr = excluded.title_tr, title_target = excluded.title_target, cefr_level = excluded.cefr_level, summary_tr = excluded.summary_tr, examples = excluded.examples, practice_items = excluded.practice_items, order_index = excluded.order_index;
• There is + tekil veya sayılamayan: There is a park near here. There is some milk.
• There are + çoğul: There are two chairs.
• Olumsuz: There isn’t / There aren’t (any …).
• Soru: Is there …? / Are there …? Kısa cevap: Yes, there is. / No, there aren’t.
• Soruda ve olumsuzda “any” kullanılır: Are there any shops?', '[{"text":"There is a bank next to the school.","tr":"Okulun yanında bir banka var.","highlight":"There is"},{"text":"There are three books on the desk.","tr":"Masanın üstünde üç kitap var.","highlight":"There are"},{"text":"There isn’t any milk.","tr":"Hiç süt yok.","highlight":"There isn’t any"},{"text":"Is there a bus stop near here?","tr":"Buraya yakın otobüs durağı var mı?","highlight":"Is there"}]'::jsonb, '[{"type":"mcq","prompt":"___ a cinema in my town.","options":["There are","There is","It are","Is there"],"answer":1},{"type":"mcq","prompt":"___ two cats in the garden.","options":["There is","There are","There be","Is there"],"answer":1,"explain_tr":"Çoğul isimle “There are”."},{"type":"fill","prompt":"Are there ___ eggs? (some/any)","answer":"any","explain_tr":"Soru ve olumsuzda any kullanılır."},{"type":"fill","prompt":"___ there a toilet here? (Is/Are)","answer":"Is","explain_tr":"Tekil isim: Is there…?"},{"type":"mcq","prompt":"There ___ any water in the bottle.","options":["aren’t","isn’t","not is","don’t"],"answer":1,"explain_tr":"water sayılamayandır → isn’t."}]'::jsonb, 4) on conflict (language_code, slug) do update set title_tr = excluded.title_tr, title_target = excluded.title_target, cefr_level = excluded.cefr_level, summary_tr = excluded.summary_tr, examples = excluded.examples, practice_items = excluded.practice_items, order_index = excluded.order_index;
• Düzenli fiiller: fiil + -ed (walk → walked)
• Düzensiz fiiller ezberlenir (go → went, have → had, see → saw)
• Olumsuz: did not (didn''t) + fiilin yalın hali: I didn''t go.
• Soru: Did + özne + yalın fiil? Did you go?

Zaman ifadeleri: yesterday, last week, two days ago, in 2019.', '[{"text":"We walked to school.","tr":"Okula yürüdük.","highlight":"walked"},{"text":"She went to Paris last year.","tr":"Geçen yıl Paris''e gitti.","highlight":"went"},{"text":"I didn''t see him.","tr":"Onu görmedim.","highlight":"didn''t see"},{"text":"Did you enjoy the film?","tr":"Filmden hoşlandın mı?","highlight":"Did you enjoy"}]'::jsonb, '[{"type":"mcq","prompt":"Yesterday I ___ a new phone.","options":["buy","buyed","bought","buying"],"answer":2,"explain_tr":"buy düzensizdir: buy → bought."},{"type":"mcq","prompt":"She ___ to the party last night.","options":["didn''t went","didn''t go","not go","doesn''t go"],"answer":1,"explain_tr":"did not''tan sonra yalın fiil gelir."},{"type":"fill","prompt":"We ___ (watch) a film last night.","answer":"watched"},{"type":"fill","prompt":"They ___ (go) to Spain in 2022.","answer":"went"},{"type":"fill","prompt":"___ you see the match yesterday? (Did/Do/Are)","answer":"did"}]'::jsonb, 5) on conflict (language_code, slug) do update set title_tr = excluded.title_tr, title_target = excluded.title_target, cefr_level = excluded.cefr_level, summary_tr = excluded.summary_tr, examples = excluded.examples, practice_items = excluded.practice_items, order_index = excluded.order_index;
• I am working. / She is reading. / They are playing.
• Olumsuz: I’m not, he isn’t, we aren’t + fiil-ing.
• Soru: Are you listening?
• Yakın planlı gelecek için de kullanılır: I’m meeting Ali tomorrow.
• Durum fiilleri (know, like, want, understand) genelde -ing almaz: I know him. (I’m knowing değil)
• Yazım: make → making, run → running.', '[{"text":"I am studying English now.","tr":"Şu an İngilizce çalışıyorum.","highlight":"am studying"},{"text":"She is cooking dinner.","tr":"O akşam yemeği pişiriyor.","highlight":"is cooking"},{"text":"They aren’t watching TV.","tr":"Onlar televizyon izlemiyor.","highlight":"aren’t watching"},{"text":"We are meeting Anna on Friday.","tr":"Cuma günü Anna ile buluşuyoruz.","highlight":"are meeting"}]'::jsonb, '[{"type":"mcq","prompt":"Look! It ___ .","options":["rains","is raining","rain","raining"],"answer":1,"explain_tr":"Şu an olan olay: is raining."},{"type":"mcq","prompt":"Why ___ you laughing?","options":["is","are","do","am"],"answer":1},{"type":"fill","prompt":"He ___ not sleeping at the moment. (is/are)","answer":"is","explain_tr":"he ile is."},{"type":"fill","prompt":"They are ___ football now. (play)","answer":"playing","explain_tr":"am/is/are + fiil-ing."},{"type":"mcq","prompt":"Which sentence is correct?","options":["I am knowing the answer.","I know the answer.","I am know the answer.","I knowing the answer."],"answer":1,"explain_tr":"know bir durum fiilidir; -ing almaz."}]'::jsonb, 6) on conflict (language_code, slug) do update set title_tr = excluded.title_tr, title_target = excluded.title_target, cefr_level = excluded.cefr_level, summary_tr = excluded.summary_tr, examples = excluded.examples, practice_items = excluded.practice_items, order_index = excluded.order_index;
• Uzun sıfatlarda more / the most: more expensive than, the most expensive.
• -y ile biten: easy → easier → the easiest. Tek heceli, sessiz-sesli-sessiz: big → bigger → the biggest.
• Düzensizler: good → better → the best; bad → worse → the worst; far → farther → the farthest.
• Eşitlik: as … as → She is as tall as me.', '[{"text":"My bag is heavier than yours.","tr":"Benim çantam seninkinden daha ağır.","highlight":"heavier than"},{"text":"This is the most interesting book.","tr":"Bu en ilginç kitap.","highlight":"the most interesting"},{"text":"Today is better than yesterday.","tr":"Bugün dünden daha iyi.","highlight":"better than"},{"text":"He is as tall as his father.","tr":"Babası kadar uzun.","highlight":"as tall as"}]'::jsonb, '[{"type":"mcq","prompt":"A train is ___ a bus.","options":["fast than","faster than","more fast than","fastest than"],"answer":1},{"type":"mcq","prompt":"This is ___ restaurant in town.","options":["the better","the best","the most good","best"],"answer":1,"explain_tr":"good → better → the best."},{"type":"fill","prompt":"London is ___ expensive than Ankara. (more/most)","answer":"more","explain_tr":"Uzun sıfat: more … than."},{"type":"fill","prompt":"She is the ___ girl in the class. (tall)","answer":"tallest","explain_tr":"Kısa sıfat üstünlük: the -est."},{"type":"mcq","prompt":"Which sentence is correct?","options":["It is more cheaper.","It is cheaper.","It is the cheaper than.","It is cheapest than."],"answer":1}]'::jsonb, 7) on conflict (language_code, slug) do update set title_tr = excluded.title_tr, title_target = excluded.title_target, cefr_level = excluded.cefr_level, summary_tr = excluded.summary_tr, examples = excluded.examples, practice_items = excluded.practice_items, order_index = excluded.order_index;
• at → saat ve belirli anlar: at 8 o’clock, at night, at the weekend
• on → günler ve tarihler: on Monday, on 5 May, on my birthday
• in → ay, mevsim, yıl, günün bölümleri: in July, in summer, in 2024, in the morning
Yer:
• at → nokta: at the bus stop, at home, at work
• on → yüzey: on the table, on the wall
• in → kapalı alan, şehir, ülke: in the room, in Istanbul, in Turkey', '[{"text":"The class starts at 9 o’clock.","tr":"Ders saat 9’da başlıyor.","highlight":"at 9 o’clock"},{"text":"My birthday is on 12 June.","tr":"Doğum günüm 12 Haziran’da.","highlight":"on 12 June"},{"text":"We go skiing in winter.","tr":"Kışın kayak yapmaya gidiyoruz.","highlight":"in winter"},{"text":"The keys are on the table.","tr":"Anahtarlar masanın üstünde.","highlight":"on the table"}]'::jsonb, '[{"type":"mcq","prompt":"I always get up ___ 7 o’clock.","options":["in","on","at","to"],"answer":2},{"type":"mcq","prompt":"We have a meeting ___ Tuesday.","options":["in","at","on","by"],"answer":2},{"type":"fill","prompt":"She was born ___ 1998. (in/on/at)","answer":"in","explain_tr":"Yıllarla in kullanılır."},{"type":"fill","prompt":"I’m waiting ___ the bus stop. (in/on/at)","answer":"at","explain_tr":"Belirli bir nokta için at."},{"type":"mcq","prompt":"They live ___ Germany.","options":["at","on","in","to"],"answer":2,"explain_tr":"Ülkelerle in kullanılır."}]'::jsonb, 8) on conflict (language_code, slug) do update set title_tr = excluded.title_tr, title_target = excluded.title_target, cefr_level = excluded.cefr_level, summary_tr = excluded.summary_tr, examples = excluded.examples, practice_items = excluded.practice_items, order_index = excluded.order_index;
• Sayılamayan isimler sayılmaz: water, milk, money, information, advice. Çoğulu yoktur ve tekil fiil alır: The information is useful.
• many + sayılabilir çoğul: How many books? / much + sayılamayan: How much water?
• a lot of / lots of her ikisiyle olumlu cümlede kullanılır.
• a few + sayılabilir (birkaç), a little + sayılamayan (biraz).', '[{"text":"How many students are there?","tr":"Kaç öğrenci var?","highlight":"How many"},{"text":"We don’t have much time.","tr":"Fazla zamanımız yok.","highlight":"much time"},{"text":"I need a little sugar.","tr":"Biraz şekere ihtiyacım var.","highlight":"a little sugar"},{"text":"She has a lot of friends.","tr":"Çok arkadaşı var.","highlight":"a lot of"}]'::jsonb, '[{"type":"mcq","prompt":"How ___ money do you need?","options":["many","much","few","a few"],"answer":1,"explain_tr":"money sayılamaz → much."},{"type":"mcq","prompt":"There are only ___ chairs in the room.","options":["a little","much","a few","a lot"],"answer":2},{"type":"fill","prompt":"I don’t have ___ friends here. (much/many)","answer":"many","explain_tr":"friends sayılabilir çoğul → many."},{"type":"fill","prompt":"Can I have ___ water, please? (a few/a little)","answer":"a little","explain_tr":"water sayılamaz → a little."},{"type":"mcq","prompt":"Which sentence is correct?","options":["The informations are useful.","The information is useful.","The information are useful.","An information is useful."],"answer":1,"explain_tr":"information sayılamaz; çoğulu yoktur."}]'::jsonb, 9) on conflict (language_code, slug) do update set title_tr = excluded.title_tr, title_target = excluded.title_target, cefr_level = excluded.cefr_level, summary_tr = excluded.summary_tr, examples = excluded.examples, practice_items = excluded.practice_items, order_index = excluded.order_index;
• will → konuşma anında verilen karar, söz, teklif, tahmin: I’ll help you. I think it will be sunny.
• will + yalın fiil; olumsuz: won’t. Soru: Will you come?
• Sözle verilen vaatlerde ve “I think / probably” sonrasında will kullanılır.', '[{"text":"I’m going to visit my aunt this weekend.","tr":"Bu hafta sonu teyzemi ziyaret edeceğim.","highlight":"I’m going to visit"},{"text":"The phone is ringing. I’ll answer it.","tr":"Telefon çalıyor. Ben açarım.","highlight":"I’ll answer"},{"text":"She will probably be late.","tr":"Muhtemelen geç kalacak.","highlight":"will probably be"},{"text":"We won’t forget your birthday.","tr":"Doğum gününü unutmayacağız.","highlight":"won’t forget"}]'::jsonb, '[{"type":"mcq","prompt":"“We have no milk.” – “OK, I ___ buy some.”","options":["am going to","will","buy","am buying to"],"answer":1,"explain_tr":"Anlık karar → will."},{"type":"mcq","prompt":"Look at that car! It ___ crash.","options":["will","is going to","goes to","is going"],"answer":1,"explain_tr":"Gözle görülen kanıt → going to."},{"type":"fill","prompt":"I think it ___ rain tomorrow. (will/won’t – olumlu)","answer":"will"},{"type":"fill","prompt":"He ___ going to start a new job in May. (is/are)","answer":"is","explain_tr":"he ile is going to."},{"type":"mcq","prompt":"Which sentence is correct?","options":["She will to call you.","She will call you.","She wills call you.","She will calls you."],"answer":1,"explain_tr":"will + yalın fiil."}]'::jsonb, 10) on conflict (language_code, slug) do update set title_tr = excluded.title_tr, title_target = excluded.title_target, cefr_level = excluded.cefr_level, summary_tr = excluded.summary_tr, examples = excluded.examples, practice_items = excluded.practice_items, order_index = excluded.order_index;
• Deneyim: I have been to Italy. (Ne zaman olduğu söylenmez.)
• Sonucu şimdi görülen olay: I have lost my keys.
• Süren durum: She has lived here for five years / since 2019.
• for + süre, since + başlangıç noktası. ever, never, already, yet, just sık kullanılır.
• Belirli geçmiş zaman (yesterday, in 2010, last week) varsa past simple gerekir: I went there last week.', '[{"text":"I have visited Berlin twice.","tr":"Berlin’i iki kez ziyaret ettim.","highlight":"have visited"},{"text":"She has lived here since 2020.","tr":"2020’den beri burada yaşıyor.","highlight":"has lived"},{"text":"Have you ever eaten sushi?","tr":"Hiç suşi yedin mi?","highlight":"Have you ever eaten"},{"text":"They haven’t finished yet.","tr":"Daha bitirmediler.","highlight":"haven’t finished"}]'::jsonb, '[{"type":"mcq","prompt":"I ___ my homework already.","options":["did","have done","has done","am doing"],"answer":1},{"type":"mcq","prompt":"He has worked here ___ 2018.","options":["for","since","from","during"],"answer":1,"explain_tr":"Başlangıç noktası → since."},{"type":"fill","prompt":"We have lived here ___ ten years. (for/since)","answer":"for","explain_tr":"Süre → for."},{"type":"fill","prompt":"She ___ never been to Spain. (have/has)","answer":"has","explain_tr":"she ile has."},{"type":"mcq","prompt":"Which sentence is correct?","options":["I have seen him yesterday.","I saw him yesterday.","I have saw him yesterday.","I seen him yesterday."],"answer":1,"explain_tr":"yesterday ile past simple kullanılır."}]'::jsonb, 11) on conflict (language_code, slug) do update set title_tr = excluded.title_tr, title_target = excluded.title_target, cefr_level = excluded.cefr_level, summary_tr = excluded.summary_tr, examples = excluded.examples, practice_items = excluded.practice_items, order_index = excluded.order_index;
• mustn’t → yasak (yapma!): You mustn’t smoke here. 
• don’t have to → zorunlu değil (gerek yok): You don’t have to come.
• should / shouldn’t → tavsiye: You should see a doctor.
• Modallerden sonra fiil yalın gelir ve -s almaz: She must go. Soru/olumsuz için do kullanılmaz (should, must); have to için do/does gerekir.', '[{"text":"You must wear a seat belt.","tr":"Emniyet kemeri takmak zorundasın.","highlight":"must wear"},{"text":"I have to get up early tomorrow.","tr":"Yarın erken kalkmak zorundayım.","highlight":"have to get up"},{"text":"You don’t have to pay.","tr":"Ödemek zorunda değilsin.","highlight":"don’t have to pay"},{"text":"You should drink more water.","tr":"Daha çok su içmelisin.","highlight":"should drink"}]'::jsonb, '[{"type":"mcq","prompt":"Students ___ use phones in the exam. It is forbidden.","options":["don’t have to","mustn’t","shouldn’t to","haven’t"],"answer":1,"explain_tr":"Yasak anlamı: mustn’t."},{"type":"mcq","prompt":"It’s Sunday. I ___ go to work.","options":["must","don’t have to","mustn’t","should to"],"answer":1,"explain_tr":"Zorunlu değil → don’t have to."},{"type":"fill","prompt":"She ___ to wear glasses. (has/have)","answer":"has","explain_tr":"she ile has to."},{"type":"fill","prompt":"You look tired. You ___ go to bed early. (should/must to)","answer":"should","explain_tr":"Tavsiye → should."},{"type":"mcq","prompt":"Which sentence is correct?","options":["He musts go.","He must goes.","He must go.","He must to go."],"answer":2}]'::jsonb, 12) on conflict (language_code, slug) do update set title_tr = excluded.title_tr, title_target = excluded.title_target, cefr_level = excluded.cefr_level, summary_tr = excluded.summary_tr, examples = excluded.examples, practice_items = excluded.practice_items, order_index = excluded.order_index;
• Present: The room is cleaned every day.
• Past: The window was broken last night.
• Will: The report will be finished tomorrow.
• Yapanı belirtmek için by: The book was written by Orwell.
• Soru: Was the window broken? Olumsuz: It wasn’t found.
• Aktif → Pasif: Someone stole my bike. → My bike was stolen.', '[{"text":"English is spoken all over the world.","tr":"İngilizce dünyanın her yerinde konuşulur.","highlight":"is spoken"},{"text":"The museum was built in 1900.","tr":"Müze 1900’de yapıldı.","highlight":"was built"},{"text":"The letters will be sent tomorrow.","tr":"Mektuplar yarın gönderilecek.","highlight":"will be sent"},{"text":"This song was written by my brother.","tr":"Bu şarkıyı kardeşim yazdı.","highlight":"was written by"}]'::jsonb, '[{"type":"mcq","prompt":"The cake ___ by my mother.","options":["made","was made","was make","is making"],"answer":1},{"type":"mcq","prompt":"Cars ___ in this factory.","options":["is produced","are produced","produce","are produce"],"answer":1,"explain_tr":"Çoğul özne: are produced."},{"type":"fill","prompt":"The thief ___ caught yesterday. (was/were)","answer":"was","explain_tr":"Tekil özne: was caught."},{"type":"fill","prompt":"The bridge was ___ in 2010. (build)","answer":"built","explain_tr":"build → built (V3)."},{"type":"mcq","prompt":"“Someone stole my wallet.” → ","options":["My wallet stole.","My wallet was stolen.","My wallet is stole.","My wallet was stealing."],"answer":1}]'::jsonb, 13) on conflict (language_code, slug) do update set title_tr = excluded.title_tr, title_target = excluded.title_target, cefr_level = excluded.cefr_level, summary_tr = excluded.summary_tr, examples = excluded.examples, practice_items = excluded.practice_items, order_index = excluded.order_index;
• who → kişiler: The man who lives next door is a doctor.
• which → nesneler: The book which I bought is great.
• that → hem kişi hem nesne için (günlük konuşmada sık): The film that we saw was funny.
• where → yer: This is the café where we met.
• Nesne konumundaki who/which/that atılabilir: The book (that) I bought…
• Özne konumunda atılamaz: The man who called you is here.', '[{"text":"The woman who works here is my aunt.","tr":"Burada çalışan kadın teyzem.","highlight":"who works here"},{"text":"This is the phone which I lost.","tr":"Bu, kaybettiğim telefon.","highlight":"which I lost"},{"text":"That is the school where I studied.","tr":"Orası okuduğum okul.","highlight":"where I studied"},{"text":"The film that we watched was boring.","tr":"İzlediğimiz film sıkıcıydı.","highlight":"that we watched"}]'::jsonb, '[{"type":"mcq","prompt":"The girl ___ is sitting there is my sister.","options":["which","who","where","whose is"],"answer":1,"explain_tr":"Kişi için who."},{"type":"mcq","prompt":"This is the town ___ I grew up.","options":["who","which","where","what"],"answer":2,"explain_tr":"Yer için where."},{"type":"fill","prompt":"The car ___ I bought is red. (who/which)","answer":"which","explain_tr":"Nesne için which (veya that)."},{"type":"fill","prompt":"The man ___ called you is my boss. (who/where)","answer":"who","explain_tr":"Kişi → who."},{"type":"mcq","prompt":"Which sentence is correct?","options":["The book who I read is good.","The book which I read it is good.","The book that I read is good.","The book where I read is good."],"answer":2}]'::jsonb, 14) on conflict (language_code, slug) do update set title_tr = excluded.title_tr, title_target = excluded.title_target, cefr_level = excluded.cefr_level, summary_tr = excluded.summary_tr, examples = excluded.examples, practice_items = excluded.practice_items, order_index = excluded.order_index;
If + present simple, will + yalın fiil

If it rains, we will stay at home.

Dikkat: “if” bölümünde will kullanılmaz. Sıralama değişebilir: We will stay at home if it rains (virgül gerekmez).', '[{"text":"If you study, you will pass the exam.","tr":"Çalışırsan sınavı geçersin.","highlight":"If you study, you will pass"},{"text":"If it rains, we will stay at home.","tr":"Yağmur yağarsa evde kalırız.","highlight":"If it rains, we will stay"},{"text":"She will be happy if you call her.","tr":"Onu ararsan mutlu olur.","highlight":"will be happy if you call"}]'::jsonb, '[{"type":"mcq","prompt":"If I ___ time tomorrow, I will call you.","options":["have","will have","had","would have"],"answer":0,"explain_tr":"if bölümünde şimdiki zaman kullanılır."},{"type":"mcq","prompt":"If she ___ late, we will start without her.","options":["will be","is","was","would be"],"answer":1},{"type":"fill","prompt":"If it snows, the school ___ (close). Use will.","answer":"will close","explain_tr":"“will + yalın fiil”."},{"type":"fill","prompt":"We will go to the beach if the weather ___ (be) nice.","answer":"is"},{"type":"mcq","prompt":"Which sentence is correct?","options":["If he will come, I will be happy.","If he comes, I will be happy.","If he came, I will be happy.","If he comes, I would be happy."],"answer":1}]'::jsonb, 15) on conflict (language_code, slug) do update set title_tr = excluded.title_tr, title_target = excluded.title_target, cefr_level = excluded.cefr_level, summary_tr = excluded.summary_tr, examples = excluded.examples, practice_items = excluded.practice_items, order_index = excluded.order_index;
• If + past simple, would + yalın fiil → If I had more money, I would travel the world.
• “be” fiilinde tüm özneler için “were” kullanılabilir: If I were you, I would call him.
• would yerine could / might da kullanılabilir.
• Gerçekleşmesi olası durumlar için first conditional: If it rains, I will stay home.', '[{"text":"If I won the lottery, I would buy a house.","tr":"Piyangoyu kazansam bir ev alırdım.","highlight":"If I won"},{"text":"If I were you, I would accept the job.","tr":"Senin yerinde olsam işi kabul ederdim.","highlight":"If I were you"},{"text":"She would help us if she had time.","tr":"Zamanı olsa bize yardım ederdi.","highlight":"would help"},{"text":"What would you do if you lost your passport?","tr":"Pasaportunu kaybetsen ne yapardın?","highlight":"would you do"}]'::jsonb, '[{"type":"mcq","prompt":"If I ___ rich, I would help everyone.","options":["am","was being","were","will be"],"answer":2},{"type":"mcq","prompt":"If she studied more, she ___ the exam.","options":["will pass","would pass","passes","would passed"],"answer":1},{"type":"fill","prompt":"If I ___ you, I would talk to her. (be)","answer":"were","explain_tr":"Tavsiyede were kullanılır."},{"type":"fill","prompt":"He would travel more if he ___ time. (have)","answer":"had","explain_tr":"if + past simple: had."},{"type":"mcq","prompt":"Which sentence is correct?","options":["If I would know, I would tell you.","If I knew, I would tell you.","If I know, I would tell you.","If I knew, I will tell you."],"answer":1}]'::jsonb, 16) on conflict (language_code, slug) do update set title_tr = excluded.title_tr, title_target = excluded.title_target, cefr_level = excluded.cefr_level, summary_tr = excluded.summary_tr, examples = excluded.examples, practice_items = excluded.practice_items, order_index = excluded.order_index;
• am/is/are → was/were; present simple → past simple; present continuous → past continuous
• present perfect / past simple → past perfect; will → would; can → could
• Zamir ve zaman ifadeleri değişir: today → that day, tomorrow → the next day, now → then, here → there.
• said / told: He said that… ; He told me that… (told + kişi).
• Sorular: dolaylıda düz cümle sırası kullanılır: She asked where I lived. Evet/hayır sorularında if/whether: He asked if I was ready.', '[{"text":"She said that she was tired.","tr":"“Yorgunum” dedi.","highlight":"she was tired"},{"text":"He told me that he would call me.","tr":"Beni arayacağını söyledi.","highlight":"would call"},{"text":"They said they had finished.","tr":"Bitirdiklerini söylediler.","highlight":"had finished"},{"text":"He asked me where I lived.","tr":"Nerede yaşadığımı sordu.","highlight":"where I lived"}]'::jsonb, '[{"type":"mcq","prompt":"“I am hungry,” he said. → He said that he ___ hungry.","options":["is","was","were","has been"],"answer":1},{"type":"mcq","prompt":"“I will help you,” she said. → She said she ___ help me.","options":["will","would","did","can"],"answer":1},{"type":"fill","prompt":"“I live in Rome,” he said. → He said that he ___ in Rome. (live)","answer":"lived","explain_tr":"Present simple → past simple."},{"type":"fill","prompt":"“Where do you work?” → She asked me where I ___. (work)","answer":"worked","explain_tr":"Dolaylı soruda düz cümle sırası ve past simple."},{"type":"mcq","prompt":"Which sentence is correct?","options":["He told that he was ill.","He told me that he was ill.","He said me that he was ill.","He told to me he was ill."],"answer":1,"explain_tr":"told + kişi; said ile kişi doğrudan gelmez."}]'::jsonb, 17) on conflict (language_code, slug) do update set title_tr = excluded.title_tr, title_target = excluded.title_target, cefr_level = excluded.cefr_level, summary_tr = excluded.summary_tr, examples = excluded.examples, practice_items = excluded.practice_items, order_index = excluded.order_index;
• When I arrived, the film had already started. (Önce film başladı, sonra ben geldim.)
• Genellikle past simple ile birlikte: after, before, when, by the time, already, just.
• Olumsuz: hadn’t + V3. Soru: Had you finished…?
• Reported speech’te present perfect ve past simple’ın geri adımı: “I have seen it.” → He said he had seen it.', '[{"text":"When we arrived, the train had left.","tr":"Vardığımızda tren gitmişti.","highlight":"had left"},{"text":"She was tired because she hadn’t slept.","tr":"Uyumadığı için yorgundu.","highlight":"hadn’t slept"},{"text":"I had never seen snow before I moved to Canada.","tr":"Kanada’ya taşınmadan önce hiç kar görmemiştim.","highlight":"had never seen"},{"text":"After he had eaten, he went to bed.","tr":"Yemek yedikten sonra yattı.","highlight":"had eaten"}]'::jsonb, '[{"type":"mcq","prompt":"By the time I got home, my family ___ dinner.","options":["has eaten","had eaten","ate","was eaten"],"answer":1},{"type":"mcq","prompt":"I was late because I ___ my keys.","options":["lost","had lost","have lost","was losing"],"answer":1},{"type":"fill","prompt":"She ___ already left when I called. (had/has)","answer":"had","explain_tr":"Önce olan olay: had left."},{"type":"fill","prompt":"They ___ never met before the party. (had/have)","answer":"had","explain_tr":"Geçmişteki bir anın öncesi: had never met."},{"type":"mcq","prompt":"Which sentence is correct?","options":["When he came, we have finished.","When he came, we had finished.","When he came, we finish.","When he came, we had finish."],"answer":1}]'::jsonb, 18) on conflict (language_code, slug) do update set title_tr = excluded.title_tr, title_target = excluded.title_target, cefr_level = excluded.cefr_level, summary_tr = excluded.summary_tr, examples = excluded.examples, practice_items = excluded.practice_items, order_index = excluded.order_index;
• If + past perfect, would have + V3 → If I had studied, I would have passed.
• would yerine could have / might have da kullanılabilir.
• Olumsuz: If I hadn’t missed the bus, I wouldn’t have been late.
• Koşul ve sonuç yer değiştirebilir: I would have called you if I had known.', '[{"text":"If I had known, I would have helped you.","tr":"Bilseydim sana yardım ederdim.","highlight":"If I had known"},{"text":"If she hadn’t been late, she would have caught the train.","tr":"Geç kalmasaydı trene yetişirdi.","highlight":"hadn’t been late"},{"text":"We would have won if we had played better.","tr":"Daha iyi oynasaydık kazanırdık.","highlight":"would have won"},{"text":"What would you have done if you had missed your flight?","tr":"Uçağını kaçırsaydın ne yapardın?","highlight":"would you have done"}]'::jsonb, '[{"type":"mcq","prompt":"If I ___ earlier, I would have caught the bus.","options":["left","had left","would leave","have left"],"answer":1},{"type":"mcq","prompt":"If he had studied, he ___ the exam.","options":["would pass","would have passed","passed","had passed"],"answer":1},{"type":"fill","prompt":"If we ___ the map, we would not have got lost. (have – had formu)","answer":"had had","explain_tr":"Past perfect of have: had had."},{"type":"fill","prompt":"She would have come if she ___ about the party. (know)","answer":"had known","explain_tr":"if + past perfect."},{"type":"mcq","prompt":"Which sentence is correct?","options":["If I would have known, I would have told you.","If I had known, I would have told you.","If I knew, I would have told you.","If I had known, I will tell you."],"answer":1,"explain_tr":"if-cümlesinde “would have” kullanılmaz."}]'::jsonb, 19) on conflict (language_code, slug) do update set title_tr = excluded.title_tr, title_target = excluded.title_target, cefr_level = excluded.cefr_level, summary_tr = excluded.summary_tr, examples = excluded.examples, practice_items = excluded.practice_items, order_index = excluded.order_index;
• Never / Rarely / Seldom / Hardly / Scarcely / Not only / Under no circumstances / Only when / No sooner …
• Never have I seen such a view. · Rarely does she complain.
• Hardly had we sat down when the phone rang. (had + özne + V3 … when)
• No sooner had he left than it started to rain. (…than)
• Not only did he forget the tickets, but he also lost his passport.
• Yardımcı fiil yoksa do/does/did eklenir.', '[{"text":"Never have I seen such a beautiful view.","tr":"Hiç böylesine güzel bir manzara görmedim.","highlight":"Never have I seen"},{"text":"Rarely does she complain about work.","tr":"İşinden nadiren şikâyet eder.","highlight":"Rarely does she complain"},{"text":"Not only did he forget the tickets, but he also lost his passport.","tr":"Biletleri unutmakla kalmadı, pasaportunu da kaybetti.","highlight":"Not only did he forget"},{"text":"Hardly had we sat down when the phone rang.","tr":"Daha oturmuştuk ki telefon çaldı.","highlight":"Hardly had we sat down"}]'::jsonb, '[{"type":"mcq","prompt":"Never ___ such a delicious meal.","options":["I have eaten","have I eaten","I ate","did I eaten"],"answer":1,"explain_tr":"Never başa gelince: Never + have + özne + V3."},{"type":"mcq","prompt":"Rarely ___ late for meetings.","options":["he is","is he","does he","he does"],"answer":1,"explain_tr":"“be” fiilinde fiil özneden önce gelir: Rarely is he late."},{"type":"fill","prompt":"Not only ___ she speak French, but she also speaks Italian. (do/does/did)","answer":"does","explain_tr":"Düz cümle present simple: Not only does she speak…"},{"type":"fill","prompt":"Hardly ___ we arrived when it started to rain. (had/did)","answer":"had","explain_tr":"Hardly had + özne + V3 … when"},{"type":"mcq","prompt":"Which sentence is correct?","options":["Under no circumstances you should open this door.","Under no circumstances should you open this door.","Under no circumstances do you should open this door.","Under no circumstances should open you this door."],"answer":1}]'::jsonb, 20) on conflict (language_code, slug) do update set title_tr = excluded.title_tr, title_target = excluded.title_target, cefr_level = excluded.cefr_level, summary_tr = excluded.summary_tr, examples = excluded.examples, practice_items = excluded.practice_items, order_index = excluded.order_index;
• Karma koşul (şimdi → geçmiş): If she weren’t so shy, she would have asked for help.
• wish + past simple → şimdiki durumdan pişmanlık: I wish I had more time. (I wish I were taller.)
• wish + past perfect → geçmişten pişmanlık: I wish I had studied medicine.
• wish + would → başkasının alışkanlığından rahatsızlık: I wish you would stop interrupting.
• If only, wish ile aynı çalışır ama daha güçlüdür: If only he would listen!', '[{"text":"If I had taken that job, I would be living in Berlin now.","tr":"O işi kabul etseydim şimdi Berlin’de yaşıyor olurdum.","highlight":"I would be living"},{"text":"If she weren’t so shy, she would have asked for help.","tr":"Bu kadar utangaç olmasaydı yardım isterdi.","highlight":"she would have asked"},{"text":"I wish I had studied medicine.","tr":"Keşke tıp okusaydım.","highlight":"I wish I had studied"},{"text":"If only he would listen to me!","tr":"Keşke beni dinleseydi!","highlight":"If only he would listen"}]'::jsonb, '[{"type":"mcq","prompt":"If I ___ harder at school, I would have a better job now.","options":["studied","had studied","would study","have studied"],"answer":1,"explain_tr":"Geçmişteki sebep → şimdiki sonuç: had studied … would have."},{"type":"mcq","prompt":"I wish I ___ speak Japanese. (I can’t.)","options":["can","could","would","had"],"answer":1,"explain_tr":"Şimdiki durum için wish + past: could."},{"type":"fill","prompt":"If only I ___ more money! (have)","answer":"had","explain_tr":"Şimdiki istek: If only + past simple."},{"type":"mcq","prompt":"I wish you ___ so loudly. It annoys me.","options":["don’t talk","wouldn’t talk","didn’t talked","won’t talk"],"answer":1,"explain_tr":"Başkasının alışkanlığından rahatsızlık: wish + would."},{"type":"mcq","prompt":"Which sentence is correct?","options":["I wish I would have gone to the party.","I wish I had gone to the party.","I wish I went to the party yesterday.","I wish I have gone to the party."],"answer":1,"explain_tr":"Geçmiş pişmanlık: wish + past perfect."}]'::jsonb, 21) on conflict (language_code, slug) do update set title_tr = excluded.title_tr, title_target = excluded.title_target, cefr_level = excluded.cefr_level, summary_tr = excluded.summary_tr, examples = excluded.examples, practice_items = excluded.practice_items, order_index = excluded.order_index;
• It-cleft: It + be + vurgulanan öğe + who/that … → It was Maria who solved the problem. It is consistency that matters most.
• Kişiler için who veya that, diğerleri için that: It was in Paris that they met.
• Wh-cleft: What + özne + fiil + be + vurgulanan öğe → What I need is a long holiday. What annoys me is the noise.
• All / The only thing: All she wanted was some peace and quiet.
• Vurgulu ve yazılı üslupta sık kullanılır.', '[{"text":"It was Maria who solved the problem.","tr":"Sorunu çözen Maria’ydı.","highlight":"It was Maria who"},{"text":"It is consistency that matters most.","tr":"En çok önemli olan tutarlılıktır.","highlight":"It is consistency that"},{"text":"What I need is a long holiday.","tr":"İhtiyacım olan şey uzun bir tatil.","highlight":"What I need is"},{"text":"All she wanted was some peace and quiet.","tr":"Tek istediği biraz huzurdu.","highlight":"All she wanted was"}]'::jsonb, '[{"type":"mcq","prompt":"It was my brother ___ broke the window.","options":["who","what","whom","whose"],"answer":0},{"type":"mcq","prompt":"___ annoys me most is the noise.","options":["It","What","That","Which"],"answer":1,"explain_tr":"Wh-cleft: What annoys me most is …"},{"type":"fill","prompt":"What I really need ___ a good night’s sleep. (is/are)","answer":"is","explain_tr":"What … is + vurgulanan öğe."},{"type":"fill","prompt":"It was the manager ___ called me yesterday. (who/what)","answer":"who","explain_tr":"Kişi vurgusu: It was … who."},{"type":"mcq","prompt":"Which sentence is correct?","options":["It is the price what matters.","It is the price that matters.","What the price matters.","It is the price who matters."],"answer":1}]'::jsonb, 22) on conflict (language_code, slug) do update set title_tr = excluded.title_tr, title_target = excluded.title_target, cefr_level = excluded.cefr_level, summary_tr = excluded.summary_tr, examples = excluded.examples, practice_items = excluded.practice_items, order_index = excluded.order_index;
• -ing (eş zamanlı, etken): Walking home, I met an old friend.
• Having + V3 (önce biten eylem): Having finished the report, she went home.
• V3 (edilgen): Written in 1925, the novel is still popular.
• Olumsuz: Not knowing the answer, he stayed silent.
• Ortacın örtük öznesi ana cümlenin öznesidir: Walking home, the rain started ✗ (yağmur yürümüyor).', '[{"text":"Walking home, I bumped into an old friend.","tr":"Eve yürürken eski bir arkadaşa rastladım.","highlight":"Walking home"},{"text":"Having finished the report, she went home.","tr":"Raporu bitirince eve gitti.","highlight":"Having finished the report"},{"text":"Written in 1925, the novel is still popular.","tr":"1925’te yazılmış roman hâlâ popüler.","highlight":"Written in 1925"},{"text":"Not knowing the answer, he stayed silent.","tr":"Cevabı bilmediği için sessiz kaldı.","highlight":"Not knowing the answer"}]'::jsonb, '[{"type":"mcq","prompt":"___ the door, she noticed a letter on the floor.","options":["Open","Opening","Opened","To opened"],"answer":1},{"type":"mcq","prompt":"___ by his teacher, Tom felt confident.","options":["Encouraging","Encouraged","Having encourage","Encourage"],"answer":1,"explain_tr":"Edilgen anlam: Encouraged by …"},{"type":"fill","prompt":"___ already eaten, they declined dessert. (have – -ing biçimi)","answer":"Having","explain_tr":"Önce biten eylem: Having + V3."},{"type":"fill","prompt":"The house, ___ in 1890, is now a museum. (build)","answer":"built","explain_tr":"Edilgen ortaç: built."},{"type":"mcq","prompt":"Which sentence is correct?","options":["Having seen the film twice, I didn’t want to go again.","Seen the film twice, I didn’t want to go again.","Having see the film twice, I didn’t want to go again.","Seeing the film twice already, I didn’t wanted to go again."],"answer":0}]'::jsonb, 23) on conflict (language_code, slug) do update set title_tr = excluded.title_tr, title_target = excluded.title_target, cefr_level = excluded.cefr_level, summary_tr = excluded.summary_tr, examples = excluded.examples, practice_items = excluded.practice_items, order_index = excluded.order_index;

Ich fahre mit dem Bus zur Arbeit. Ich beginne um neun Uhr. Um zwölf Uhr esse ich mit meinen Freunden zu Mittag. Um fünf Uhr habe ich Feierabend.

Am Abend koche ich das Abendessen. Nach dem Essen lese ich ein Buch oder sehe fern. Um elf Uhr gehe ich ins Bett.', 74, 30, '[{"lemma":"das Frühstück","pos":"noun","meaning_tr":"kahvaltı","example":"Das Frühstück ist um sieben Uhr.","example_tr":"Kahvaltı saat yedide.","forms":["Frühstück"]},{"lemma":"frühstücken","pos":"verb","meaning_tr":"kahvaltı etmek","example":"Wir frühstücken zusammen.","example_tr":"Birlikte kahvaltı ederiz.","forms":["frühstücke","frühstückt","frühstücken"]},{"lemma":"das Abendessen","pos":"noun","meaning_tr":"akşam yemeği","example":"Das Abendessen ist fertig.","example_tr":"Akşam yemeği hazır.","forms":["Abendessen"]},{"lemma":"der Feierabend","pos":"noun","meaning_tr":"iş çıkışı, mesai sonu","example":"Nach Feierabend gehe ich schwimmen.","example_tr":"İş çıkışı yüzmeye giderim.","forms":["Feierabend"]}]'::jsonb, '[{"prompt":"Was trinkt Lena zum Frühstück?","options":["Kaffee","Tee","Milch","Saft"],"answer":1},{"prompt":"Wie fährt sie zur Arbeit?","options":["Mit dem Bus","Mit dem Auto","Zu Fuß","Mit dem Fahrrad"],"answer":0},{"prompt":"Wann geht sie ins Bett?","options":["Um neun Uhr","Um zehn Uhr","Um elf Uhr","Um zwölf Uhr"],"answer":2}]'::jsonb, 'DilYolu özgün içerik', 'Kişisel kullanım') on conflict (language_code, slug) do update set title = excluded.title, kind = excluded.kind, cefr_level = excluded.cefr_level, topics = excluded.topics, body = excluded.body, word_count = excluded.word_count, est_read_sec = excluded.est_read_sec, glossary = excluded.glossary, questions = excluded.questions;

Am Samstag haben wir den Hafen besucht, der mitten in der Stadt liegt. Die Aussicht war fantastisch, aber es war sehr windig! Am Nachmittag sind wir an der Elbe entlang spaziert und haben kleine Geschenke für unsere Familien gekauft.

Am Sonntag hat es geregnet, deshalb sind wir ins Museum gegangen und haben in einem traditionellen Restaurant zu Mittag gegessen. Ich habe zum ersten Mal Labskaus probiert. Es war besser, als ich erwartet hatte. Wir sind müde nach Hause gekommen, aber wir wollen beide bald wieder hinfahren.', 118, 47, '[{"lemma":"der Hafen","pos":"noun","meaning_tr":"liman","example":"Der Hafen ist sehr groß.","example_tr":"Liman çok büyük.","forms":["Hafen"]},{"lemma":"die Aussicht","pos":"noun","meaning_tr":"manzara","example":"Die Aussicht vom Turm ist toll.","example_tr":"Kuleden manzara harika.","forms":["Aussicht"]},{"lemma":"windig","pos":"adj","meaning_tr":"rüzgârlı","example":"Heute ist es windig.","example_tr":"Bugün hava rüzgârlı.","forms":["windig"]},{"lemma":"das Geschenk","pos":"noun","meaning_tr":"hediye","example":"Ich kaufe ein Geschenk für meine Schwester.","example_tr":"Kız kardeşime hediye alıyorum.","forms":["Geschenk","Geschenke"]},{"lemma":"erwarten","pos":"verb","meaning_tr":"beklemek, ummak","example":"Ich habe das nicht erwartet.","example_tr":"Bunu beklemiyordum.","forms":["erwartet","erwarten"]}]'::jsonb, '[{"prompt":"Wie sind sie nach Hamburg gereist?","options":["Mit dem Flugzeug","Mit dem Auto","Mit dem Zug","Mit dem Bus"],"answer":2},{"prompt":"Wie war das Wetter am Samstag?","options":["Regnerisch","Sehr windig","Verschneit","Heiß"],"answer":1},{"prompt":"Warum sind sie am Sonntag ins Museum gegangen?","options":["Es war kostenlos","Es hat geregnet","Sie haben sich gelangweilt","Ein Freund hat dort gearbeitet"],"answer":1},{"prompt":"Was sagt der Schreiber über Labskaus?","options":["Es war schrecklich","Es war besser als erwartet","Es war zu teuer","Er hat es nicht probiert"],"answer":1}]'::jsonb, 'DilYolu özgün içerik', 'Kişisel kullanım') on conflict (language_code, slug) do update set title = excluded.title, kind = excluded.kind, cefr_level = excluded.cefr_level, topics = excluded.topics, body = excluded.body, word_count = excluded.word_count, est_read_sec = excluded.est_read_sec, glossary = excluded.glossary, questions = excluded.questions;

Allerdings ist Homeoffice nicht frei von Problemen. Manche Beschäftigte berichten, dass sie sich isoliert fühlen, weil sie ihre Kollegen kaum noch persönlich treffen. Andere finden es schwierig, Arbeit und Privatleben zu trennen, besonders wenn der Schreibtisch im Wohnzimmer steht.

Deshalb probieren viele Firmen inzwischen ein hybrides Modell aus, bei dem die Mitarbeiter an manchen Tagen zu Hause und an anderen im Büro arbeiten. Befürworter sagen, dass dies die Vorteile beider Welten verbindet, während Kritiker darauf hinweisen, dass es sorgfältige Planung erfordert.', 133, 53, '[{"lemma":"das Privileg","pos":"noun","meaning_tr":"ayrıcalık","example":"Bildung ist ein Privileg.","example_tr":"Eğitim bir ayrıcalıktır.","forms":["Privileg"]},{"lemma":"schätzen","pos":"verb","meaning_tr":"takdir etmek, değer vermek","example":"Ich schätze deine Hilfe.","example_tr":"Yardımını takdir ediyorum.","forms":["schätzen","schätzt"]},{"lemma":"isoliert","pos":"adj","meaning_tr":"yalıtılmış, yalnızlaşmış","example":"Er fühlt sich isoliert.","example_tr":"Kendini yalnız hissediyor.","forms":["isoliert"]},{"lemma":"hybrid","pos":"adj","meaning_tr":"karma, hibrit","example":"Ein hybrides Auto nutzt zwei Energiequellen.","example_tr":"Hibrit araba iki enerji kaynağı kullanır.","forms":["hybrides","hybrid"]},{"lemma":"der Vorteil","pos":"noun","meaning_tr":"avantaj","example":"Das hat viele Vorteile.","example_tr":"Bunun birçok avantajı var.","forms":["Vorteil","Vorteile","Vorteilen"]}]'::jsonb, '[{"prompt":"Warum schätzen Mitarbeiter das Homeoffice?","options":["Sie verdienen mehr","Sie sparen Zeit und Geld beim Pendeln","Sie haben kürzere Tage","Sie bekommen kostenlose Geräte"],"answer":1},{"prompt":"Welches Problem wird genannt?","options":["Langsames Internet","Sich isoliert fühlen","Fehlende Computer","Hohe Miete"],"answer":1},{"prompt":"Was ist ein hybrides Modell?","options":["Nur im Büro arbeiten","Nur zu Hause arbeiten","An manchen Tagen zu Hause, an anderen im Büro arbeiten","Nachts arbeiten"],"answer":2},{"prompt":"Was sagen Kritiker über das hybride Modell?","options":["Es ist zu billig","Es erfordert sorgfältige Planung","Es funktioniert nie","Es ist illegal"],"answer":1}]'::jsonb, 'DilYolu özgün içerik', 'Kişisel kullanım') on conflict (language_code, slug) do update set title = excluded.title, kind = excluded.kind, cefr_level = excluded.cefr_level, topics = excluded.topics, body = excluded.body, word_count = excluded.word_count, est_read_sec = excluded.est_read_sec, glossary = excluded.glossary, questions = excluded.questions;

Die Folgen von chronischem Schlafmangel sind gut dokumentiert. Menschen, die regelmäßig weniger als sechs Stunden schlafen, leiden häufiger an Herzkrankheiten, nehmen eher zu und haben Konzentrationsprobleme. Vielleicht noch überraschender: Schon eine einzige schlechte Nacht kann das Urteilsvermögen in einem Maß beeinträchtigen, das mit leichter Trunkenheit vergleichbar ist.

Experten empfehlen daher, feste Zeiten einzuhalten, vor dem Schlafengehen auf Bildschirme zu verzichten und am Nachmittag weniger Koffein zu trinken. Solche Maßnahmen klingen unspektakulär, doch wenn man sie konsequent befolgt, können sie sowohl für die Gesundheit als auch für die Leistungsfähigkeit viel bewirken.', 139, 56, '[{"lemma":"verlockend","pos":"adj","meaning_tr":"cazip","example":"Das Angebot ist verlockend.","example_tr":"Teklif cazip.","forms":["verlockend"]},{"lemma":"ausreichend","pos":"adj","meaning_tr":"yeterli","example":"Wir haben ausreichend Essen.","example_tr":"Yeterince yiyeceğimiz var.","forms":["ausreichender","ausreichend"]},{"lemma":"festigen","pos":"verb","meaning_tr":"pekiştirmek, sağlamlaştırmak","example":"Schlaf festigt das Gedächtnis.","example_tr":"Uyku hafızayı pekiştirir.","forms":["festigt","festigen"]},{"lemma":"chronisch","pos":"adj","meaning_tr":"kronik","example":"Sie hat chronische Rückenschmerzen.","example_tr":"Kronik sırt ağrıları var.","forms":["chronischem","chronisch"]},{"lemma":"beeinträchtigen","pos":"verb","meaning_tr":"olumsuz etkilemek, zayıflatmak","example":"Lärm kann die Konzentration beeinträchtigen.","example_tr":"Gürültü konsantrasyonu bozabilir.","forms":["beeinträchtigen","beeinträchtigt"]}]'::jsonb, '[{"prompt":"Was tut der Schlaf laut erstem Absatz für das Gehirn?","options":["Er lässt es wachsen","Er festigt Erinnerungen und stellt das emotionale Gleichgewicht her","Er beschleunigt Reaktionen","Er ersetzt das Essen"],"answer":1},{"prompt":"Was kann laut Text schon eine schlechte Nacht bewirken?","options":["Herzkrankheiten heilen","Das Urteilsvermögen beeinträchtigen","Das Gedächtnis verbessern","Nur den Appetit steigern"],"answer":1},{"prompt":"Welcher Rat wird NICHT genannt?","options":["Feste Zeiten einhalten","Auf Bildschirme vor dem Schlafen verzichten","Nachmittags weniger Koffein trinken","Jeden Morgen Sport treiben"],"answer":3,"explain_tr":"Morgen sporu metinde geçmiyor."}]'::jsonb, 'DilYolu özgün içerik', 'Kişisel kullanım') on conflict (language_code, slug) do update set title = excluded.title, kind = excluded.kind, cefr_level = excluded.cefr_level, topics = excluded.topics, body = excluded.body, word_count = excluded.word_count, est_read_sec = excluded.est_read_sec, glossary = excluded.glossary, questions = excluded.questions;

Manche Unternehmen reagieren darauf mit festen Ruhezeiten, in denen weder E-Mails noch Anrufe zugelassen sind. Erste Erfahrungen deuten darauf hin, dass die Beschäftigten dadurch nicht nur produktiver, sondern auch zufriedener arbeiten. Dennoch bleibt die Umsetzung schwierig, solange ständige Erreichbarkeit als Zeichen von Engagement missverstanden wird.

Die Verantwortung liegt daher nicht allein beim Einzelnen. Erst wenn Organisationen eine Kultur der Aufmerksamkeit pflegen, kann sich nachhaltig etwas verändern.', 111, 44, '[{"lemma":"die Benachrichtigung","pos":"noun","meaning_tr":"bildirim","example":"Ich habe eine neue Benachrichtigung.","example_tr":"Yeni bir bildirimim var.","forms":["Benachrichtigungen"]},{"lemma":"die Unterbrechung","pos":"noun","meaning_tr":"kesinti","example":"Die Unterbrechung hat mich gestört.","example_tr":"Kesinti beni rahatsız etti."},{"lemma":"belasten","pos":"verb","meaning_tr":"yüklemek, zorlamak","example":"Der Lärm belastet mich.","example_tr":"Gürültü beni zorluyor.","forms":["belastet"]},{"lemma":"missverstehen","pos":"verb","meaning_tr":"yanlış anlamak","example":"Ich wollte nicht missverstanden werden.","example_tr":"Yanlış anlaşılmak istemedim.","forms":["missverstanden"]},{"lemma":"nachhaltig","pos":"adj","meaning_tr":"kalıcı, sürdürülebilir","example":"Wir suchen eine nachhaltige Lösung.","example_tr":"Kalıcı bir çözüm arıyoruz."}]'::jsonb, '[{"prompt":"Was gilt laut Text als knappe Ressource?","options":["Zeit im Büro","Konzentration","Geld","Strom"],"answer":1},{"prompt":"Wie reagieren manche Unternehmen?","options":["Mit festen Ruhezeiten ohne E-Mails und Anrufe","Mit längeren Arbeitszeiten","Mit weniger Personal","Mit mehr Besprechungen"],"answer":0},{"prompt":"Was erschwert die Umsetzung laut Text?","options":["Fehlende Computer","Dass ständige Erreichbarkeit als Engagement gilt","Zu hohe Gehälter","Zu wenig Urlaub"],"answer":1}]'::jsonb, 'DilYolu özgün içerik', 'Kişisel kullanım') on conflict (language_code, slug) do update set title = excluded.title, kind = excluded.kind, cefr_level = excluded.cefr_level, topics = excluded.topics, body = excluded.body, word_count = excluded.word_count, est_read_sec = excluded.est_read_sec, glossary = excluded.glossary, questions = excluded.questions;

Jetzt spiele ich sonntags für meine Familie. Meine kleine Schwester singt, und meine Eltern klatschen. Ich bin noch kein guter Gitarrist, aber es macht mir mehr Spaß als alles andere. Nächsten Monat besuche ich einen kleinen Musikkurs im Gemeindezentrum.', 94, 38, '[{"lemma":"das Hobby","pos":"noun","meaning_tr":"hobi","example":"Lesen ist mein liebstes Hobby.","example_tr":"Okumak en sevdiğim hobi."},{"lemma":"üben","pos":"verb","meaning_tr":"pratik yapmak, çalışmak","example":"Man muss jeden Tag üben.","example_tr":"Her gün pratik yapmak gerekir.","forms":["geübt"]},{"lemma":"einfach","pos":"adj","meaning_tr":"basit","example":"Das ist ein einfaches Rezept.","example_tr":"Bu basit bir tarif.","forms":["einfache"]},{"lemma":"klatschen","pos":"verb","meaning_tr":"alkışlamak","example":"Das Publikum klatscht laut.","example_tr":"Seyirci yüksek sesle alkışlıyor."},{"lemma":"das Gemeindezentrum","pos":"noun","meaning_tr":"mahalle merkezi","example":"Der Kurs ist im Gemeindezentrum.","example_tr":"Kurs mahalle merkezinde."}]'::jsonb, '[{"prompt":"Wer hat der Erzählerin das Gitarrespielen beigebracht?","options":["Ihre Schwester","Julia","Ein Musiklehrer"],"answer":1},{"prompt":"Wie lange hat sie jeden Abend geübt?","options":["Zehn Minuten","Zwanzig Minuten","Eine Stunde"],"answer":1},{"prompt":"Was macht sie nächsten Monat?","options":["Eine neue Gitarre kaufen","Einen Musikkurs besuchen","In eine andere Stadt ziehen"],"answer":1}]'::jsonb, 'DilYolu özgün içerik', 'Kişisel kullanım') on conflict (language_code, slug) do update set title = excluded.title, kind = excluded.kind, cefr_level = excluded.cefr_level, topics = excluded.topics, body = excluded.body, word_count = excluded.word_count, est_read_sec = excluded.est_read_sec, glossary = excluded.glossary, questions = excluded.questions;

Allerdings ist das Homeoffice nicht perfekt. Manche fühlen sich isoliert und vermissen die Gespräche mit Kollegen. Andere können Beruf und Privatleben schwer trennen und arbeiten am Ende länger als vorher. Führungskräfte sorgen sich außerdem, dass es schwieriger ist, neue Mitarbeiter online einzuarbeiten.

Viele Firmen probieren deshalb einen Kompromiss aus: zwei oder drei Tage im Büro und den Rest zu Hause. Die meisten Beschäftigten scheinen dieses Gleichgewicht zu bevorzugen, auch wenn es von der Tätigkeit und der Person abhängt.', 133, 53, '[{"lemma":"pendeln","pos":"verb","meaning_tr":"işe gidip gelmek","example":"Ich pendle jeden Tag mit dem Zug.","example_tr":"Her gün trenle işe gidip geliyorum."},{"lemma":"sich konzentrieren","pos":"verb","meaning_tr":"odaklanmak","example":"Ich kann mich bei dem Lärm nicht konzentrieren.","example_tr":"Bu gürültüde odaklanamıyorum.","forms":["konzentrieren"]},{"lemma":"isoliert","pos":"adj","meaning_tr":"yalnız, izole","example":"Sie fühlte sich isoliert.","example_tr":"Kendini yalnız hissetti."},{"lemma":"der Kompromiss","pos":"noun","meaning_tr":"orta yol, uzlaşma","example":"Wir haben einen Kompromiss gefunden.","example_tr":"Bir orta yol bulduk."},{"lemma":"der Mitarbeiter","pos":"noun","meaning_tr":"çalışan","example":"Die Firma hat fünfzig Mitarbeiter.","example_tr":"Şirketin elli çalışanı var.","forms":["Mitarbeiter"]}]'::jsonb, '[{"prompt":"Was ist ein Vorteil für Beschäftigte?","options":["Sie verdienen mehr","Sie sparen Zeit und Geld beim Pendeln","Sie haben mehr Besprechungen"],"answer":1},{"prompt":"Welches Problem haben manche zu Hause?","options":["Das Internet ist zu langsam","Sie arbeiten länger","Sie schlafen zu viel"],"answer":1},{"prompt":"Welchen Kompromiss probieren viele Firmen?","options":["Nur Homeoffice","Zwei oder drei Tage im Büro","Kürzere Arbeitswochen"],"answer":1}]'::jsonb, 'DilYolu özgün içerik', 'Kişisel kullanım') on conflict (language_code, slug) do update set title = excluded.title, kind = excluded.kind, cefr_level = excluded.cefr_level, topics = excluded.topics, body = excluded.body, word_count = excluded.word_count, est_read_sec = excluded.est_read_sec, glossary = excluded.glossary, questions = excluded.questions;

Kritiker weisen darauf hin, dass dieser Überfluss eine Kehrseite hat. Angesichts endloser Auswahl verbringen viele Zuschauer mehr Zeit mit dem Suchen als mit dem Schauen. Zudem konkurrieren die Plattformen, die auf Abonnements angewiesen sind, erbittert um Aufmerksamkeit, und manche Produzenten spüren den Druck, einen spannenden Anfang statt einer sorgfältig entwickelten Handlung zu liefern.

Das Streaming hat auch die Wirtschaft der Branche verändert. Es hat zwar Türen für internationale Produktionen geöffnet, die früher übersehen worden wären, doch kleineren Studios fällt es schwerer, einen fairen Anteil der Gewinne zu erhalten. Ob das Modell nachhaltig ist, bleibt offen.', 153, 61, '[{"lemma":"der Überfluss","pos":"noun","meaning_tr":"bolluk","example":"Es herrscht Überfluss an Essen.","example_tr":"Bol miktarda yiyecek var."},{"lemma":"die Kehrseite","pos":"noun","meaning_tr":"olumsuz yan","example":"Die Kehrseite ist der hohe Preis.","example_tr":"Olumsuz yanı yüksek fiyat."},{"lemma":"das Abonnement","pos":"noun","meaning_tr":"abonelik","example":"Ich habe mein Abonnement gekündigt.","example_tr":"Aboneliğimi iptal ettim.","forms":["Abonnements"]},{"lemma":"erbittert","pos":"adv","meaning_tr":"şiddetle, amansızca","example":"Die Teams kämpften erbittert.","example_tr":"Takımlar amansızca mücadele etti."},{"lemma":"nachhaltig","pos":"adj","meaning_tr":"sürdürülebilir","example":"Wir brauchen eine nachhaltige Lösung.","example_tr":"Sürdürülebilir bir çözüme ihtiyacımız var."}]'::jsonb, '[{"prompt":"Wie erscheinen Serien heute oft?","options":["Eine Folge pro Monat","Ganze Serien auf einmal","Nur am Wochenende"],"answer":1},{"prompt":"Welche Kehrseite nennen Kritiker?","options":["Zu wenige Titel","Viele Zuschauer suchen lange","Die Preise sind zu niedrig"],"answer":1},{"prompt":"Warum haben kleine Studios Probleme?","options":["Sie produzieren zu viel","Sie erhalten schwerer einen fairen Anteil der Gewinne","Sie lehnen Streaming ab"],"answer":1}]'::jsonb, 'DilYolu özgün içerik', 'Kişisel kullanım') on conflict (language_code, slug) do update set title = excluded.title, kind = excluded.kind, cefr_level = excluded.cefr_level, topics = excluded.topics, body = excluded.body, word_count = excluded.word_count, est_read_sec = excluded.est_read_sec, glossary = excluded.glossary, questions = excluded.questions;

Die Erklärung liegt zum Teil in der Last der Entscheidung. Wenn die Alternativen sich vermehren, wird jede verworfene Option zu einer möglichen Quelle des Bedauerns, und man bleibt mit dem beunruhigenden Gefühl zurück, ein besseres Ergebnis wäre erreichbar gewesen. Paradoxerweise kann gerade derjenige, der aus der größten Speisekarte gewählt hat, am Ende am wenigsten zufrieden sein.

Das heißt nicht, dass Wahlfreiheit an sich schädlich ist. Vielmehr zeigt es, dass die Zufriedenheit davon abhängt, wie wir wählen. Menschen, die sich vorab klare Kriterien setzen und mit einem Ergebnis zufrieden sind, das gut genug ist, berichten tendenziell von größerem Wohlbefinden als jene, die unablässig das Optimum anstreben.', 174, 70, '[{"lemma":"die Annahme","pos":"noun","meaning_tr":"varsayım","example":"Die Theorie beruht auf einer falschen Annahme.","example_tr":"Teori yanlış bir varsayıma dayanıyor."},{"lemma":"verwirrend","pos":"adj","meaning_tr":"kafa karıştırıcı","example":"Die Speisekarte war verwirrend.","example_tr":"Menü kafa karıştırıcıydı."},{"lemma":"sich vermehren","pos":"verb","meaning_tr":"çoğalmak","example":"Die Apps vermehren sich schnell.","example_tr":"Uygulamalar hızla çoğalıyor.","forms":["vermehren"]},{"lemma":"beunruhigend","pos":"adj","meaning_tr":"huzursuz edici","example":"Es war eine beunruhigende Stille.","example_tr":"Huzursuz edici bir sessizlikti."},{"lemma":"unablässig","pos":"adv","meaning_tr":"durmaksızın","example":"Er arbeitete unablässig am Projekt.","example_tr":"Proje üzerinde durmaksızın çalıştı."}]'::jsonb, '[{"prompt":"Was zeigte das Marmeladen-Experiment?","options":["Kunden bevorzugen größere Auswahl","Kunden mit weniger Auswahl kauften häufiger","Der Preis entschied alles"],"answer":1},{"prompt":"Warum sind Menschen mit der größten Auswahl manchmal unzufriedener?","options":["Sie kaufen immer billig","Verworfene Optionen werden zur Quelle des Bedauerns","Sie mögen Einkaufen nicht"],"answer":1},{"prompt":"Was hilft der Zufriedenheit laut Text?","options":["Klare Kriterien und „gut genug“ akzeptieren","Immer das Optimum suchen","Jede Wahl vermeiden"],"answer":0}]'::jsonb, 'DilYolu özgün içerik', 'Kişisel kullanım') on conflict (language_code, slug) do update set title = excluded.title, kind = excluded.kind, cefr_level = excluded.cefr_level, topics = excluded.topics, body = excluded.body, word_count = excluded.word_count, est_read_sec = excluded.est_read_sec, glossary = excluded.glossary, questions = excluded.questions;

ich hoffe, es geht dir gut. Ich wollte fragen, ob du am Samstagabend Zeit hast. Ich plane ein kleines Abendessen bei mir um sieben Uhr, und ich würde mich sehr freuen, dich zu sehen. Hast du Lust zu kommen? Ich koche ein türkisches Gericht, das dir bestimmt schmecken wird.

Sag mir bitte Bescheid, ob du kommen kannst.

Viele Grüße
Ali', ARRAY['günlük hayat', 'yemek']::text[]) on conflict (language_code, slug) do update set cefr_level = excluded.cefr_level, kind = excluded.kind, title_tr = excluded.title_tr, prompt_tr = excluded.prompt_tr, target_phrases = excluded.target_phrases, min_words = excluded.min_words, max_words = excluded.max_words, sample_answer = excluded.sample_answer, topics = excluded.topics;
• sein (olmak): ich bin, du bist, er/sie/es ist, wir sind, ihr seid, sie/Sie sind
• haben (sahip olmak): ich habe, du hast, er/sie/es hat, wir haben, ihr habt, sie/Sie haben

Almanca’da fiil cümlede ikinci sırada durur: Ich habe einen Hund. Soruda fiil başa gelir: Hast du Hunger?', '[{"text":"Ich bin Lehrerin.","tr":"Ben öğretmenim.","highlight":"bin"},{"text":"Er hat einen Hund.","tr":"Onun bir köpeği var.","highlight":"hat"},{"text":"Wir sind müde.","tr":"Biz yorgunuz.","highlight":"sind"},{"text":"Habt ihr Hunger?","tr":"Aç mısınız?","highlight":"Habt"}]'::jsonb, '[{"type":"mcq","prompt":"Du ___ sehr nett.","options":["bin","bist","ist","seid"],"answer":1},{"type":"mcq","prompt":"Sie (onlar) ___ zwei Kinder.","options":["hat","habe","haben","habt"],"answer":2},{"type":"fill","prompt":"Ich ___ Hunger. (haben)","answer":"habe"},{"type":"fill","prompt":"Wir ___ aus der Türkei. (sein)","answer":"sind"},{"type":"mcq","prompt":"Welcher Satz ist richtig?","options":["Er haben ein Auto.","Er hat ein Auto.","Er habt ein Auto.","Er bin ein Auto."],"answer":1}]'::jsonb, 1) on conflict (language_code, slug) do update set title_tr = excluded.title_tr, title_target = excluded.title_target, cefr_level = excluded.cefr_level, summary_tr = excluded.summary_tr, examples = excluded.examples, practice_items = excluded.practice_items, order_index = excluded.order_index;
ich mache · du machst · er/sie/es macht · wir machen · ihr macht · sie/Sie machen
• Kök -t / -d ile bitiyorsa araya e girer: du arbeitest, er arbeitet.
• Bazı fiiller du ve er/sie/es ile kök ünlüsünü değiştirir: fahren → du fährst, er fährt; sprechen → du sprichst, er spricht; lesen → du liest, er liest; essen → du isst, er isst.
• “sein” ve “haben” ayrı öğrenilir: ich bin, du bist / ich habe, du hast.
• Almancada “şimdi” ve “genelde” için aynı biçim kullanılır: Ich lerne Deutsch.', '[{"text":"Ich wohne in Ankara.","tr":"Ankara’da oturuyorum.","highlight":"wohne"},{"text":"Du arbeitest viel.","tr":"Çok çalışıyorsun.","highlight":"arbeitest"},{"text":"Er fährt mit dem Bus.","tr":"O otobüsle gidiyor.","highlight":"fährt"},{"text":"Sie spricht gut Deutsch.","tr":"O iyi Almanca konuşuyor.","highlight":"spricht"}]'::jsonb, '[{"type":"mcq","prompt":"Wir ___ heute Pizza.","options":["esse","isst","essen","esst"],"answer":2,"explain_tr":"wir ile fiil mastar biçiminde kalır: essen."},{"type":"mcq","prompt":"Er ___ jeden Tag die Zeitung.","options":["lest","liest","lesen","lese"],"answer":1,"explain_tr":"lesen → er liest (e → ie)."},{"type":"fill","prompt":"Du ___ gern Kaffee. (trinken)","answer":"trinkst","explain_tr":"du ile -st eki: trinkst."},{"type":"fill","prompt":"Sie (o, tekil) ___ gut Englisch. (sprechen)","answer":"spricht","explain_tr":"sprechen → er/sie spricht (e → i)."},{"type":"mcq","prompt":"Ihr ___ sehr nett.","options":["bist","sind","seid","ist"],"answer":2,"explain_tr":"ihr ile sein: seid."}]'::jsonb, 2) on conflict (language_code, slug) do update set title_tr = excluded.title_tr, title_target = excluded.title_target, cefr_level = excluded.cefr_level, summary_tr = excluded.summary_tr, examples = excluded.examples, practice_items = excluded.practice_items, order_index = excluded.order_index;
• Cümleye zaman/yer ifadesiyle başlarsanız özne fiilden sonra gelir: Heute gehe ich ins Kino. (Heute ich gehe ✗)
• W-soruları: soru sözcüğü + fiil + özne → Wohin gehst du?
• Evet/hayır soruları: fiil başta → Gehst du ins Kino?
• Emir: fiil başta → Komm bitte her!
• Zaman – Neden – Biçim – Yer sırası (TeKaMoLo) kabaca: Ich fahre morgen mit dem Zug nach Berlin.', '[{"text":"Ich gehe heute ins Kino.","tr":"Bugün sinemaya gidiyorum.","highlight":"gehe"},{"text":"Heute gehe ich ins Kino.","tr":"Bugün sinemaya gidiyorum.","highlight":"gehe ich"},{"text":"Wohin gehst du?","tr":"Nereye gidiyorsun?","highlight":"Wohin gehst du"},{"text":"Kommst du morgen?","tr":"Yarın geliyor musun?","highlight":"Kommst du"}]'::jsonb, '[{"type":"mcq","prompt":"Morgen ___ ich nach Hamburg.","options":["fahre","ich fahre","fahren","gefahren"],"answer":0,"explain_tr":"Cümle “Morgen” ile başladığında fiil 2. sırada kalır, özne sonra gelir."},{"type":"mcq","prompt":"Welcher Satz ist richtig?","options":["Am Montag ich arbeite.","Am Montag arbeite ich.","Am Montag ich arbeiten.","Ich am Montag arbeite."],"answer":1},{"type":"fill","prompt":"___ du Kaffee? (trinken – evet/hayır sorusu)","answer":"Trinkst","explain_tr":"Evet/hayır sorusunda fiil başa gelir."},{"type":"fill","prompt":"Wo ___ du? (wohnen)","answer":"wohnst","explain_tr":"W-sorusu: soru sözcüğü + fiil + özne."},{"type":"mcq","prompt":"Welcher Satz ist richtig?","options":["Heute Abend wir sehen einen Film.","Heute Abend sehen wir einen Film.","Wir heute Abend sehen einen Film.","Sehen heute Abend wir einen Film."],"answer":1}]'::jsonb, 3) on conflict (language_code, slug) do update set title_tr = excluded.title_tr, title_target = excluded.title_target, cefr_level = excluded.cefr_level, summary_tr = excluded.summary_tr, examples = excluded.examples, practice_items = excluded.practice_items, order_index = excluded.order_index;
  kein, ein gibi çekimlenir: kein (m/n Nom.), keine (f, çoğul), keinen (m Akk.): Ich habe keinen Hund. Ich habe keine Zeit.
• nicht → fiili, sıfatı, zarfı ve belirli artikelli isimleri olumsuzlar: Ich arbeite nicht. Das ist nicht gut. Ich kenne den Mann nicht.
• nicht genellikle cümlenin sonuna yakın durur; sıfat/zarfın önüne gelir.', '[{"text":"Ich habe keine Zeit.","tr":"Zamanım yok.","highlight":"keine Zeit"},{"text":"Er hat keinen Bruder.","tr":"Erkek kardeşi yok.","highlight":"keinen Bruder"},{"text":"Ich komme heute nicht.","tr":"Bugün gelmiyorum.","highlight":"nicht"},{"text":"Das Wetter ist nicht schön.","tr":"Hava güzel değil.","highlight":"nicht schön"}]'::jsonb, '[{"type":"mcq","prompt":"Ich habe ___ Hunger.","options":["nicht","kein","keine","keinen"],"answer":3,"explain_tr":"der Hunger (m, Akk.) → keinen Hunger."},{"type":"mcq","prompt":"Das ist ___ gut.","options":["kein","keine","nicht","keinen"],"answer":2,"explain_tr":"Sıfat olumsuzlanırken nicht kullanılır."},{"type":"fill","prompt":"Wir haben ___ Auto. (kein/keine)","answer":"kein","explain_tr":"das Auto (n) → kein Auto."},{"type":"fill","prompt":"Ich habe ___ Geschwister. (kein/keine)","answer":"keine","explain_tr":"Çoğul isim → keine."},{"type":"mcq","prompt":"Welcher Satz ist richtig?","options":["Ich spreche kein Deutsch gut.","Ich spreche nicht gut Deutsch.","Ich nicht spreche Deutsch.","Ich spreche Deutsch kein."],"answer":1}]'::jsonb, 4) on conflict (language_code, slug) do update set title_tr = excluded.title_tr, title_target = excluded.title_target, cefr_level = excluded.cefr_level, summary_tr = excluded.summary_tr, examples = excluded.examples, practice_items = excluded.practice_items, order_index = excluded.order_index;
• Tekil kişilerde (ich/er) kök değişir ve ek yoktur: ich kann, du kannst, er kann · ich muss · ich will · ich darf · ich soll · ich möchte.
• Ana fiil mastar olarak CÜMLENİN SONUNA gider: Ich kann gut schwimmen. Er muss heute arbeiten.
• Olumsuz: Ich darf nicht rauchen. (yasak)  Ich muss nicht kommen. (zorunda değilim)', '[{"text":"Ich kann gut schwimmen.","tr":"İyi yüzebiliyorum.","highlight":"kann"},{"text":"Du musst heute lernen.","tr":"Bugün çalışmak zorundasın.","highlight":"musst"},{"text":"Wir wollen nach Italien fahren.","tr":"İtalya’ya gitmek istiyoruz.","highlight":"wollen"},{"text":"Hier darf man nicht rauchen.","tr":"Burada sigara içmek yasak.","highlight":"darf man nicht rauchen"}]'::jsonb, '[{"type":"mcq","prompt":"Ich ___ heute nicht kommen. Ich bin krank.","options":["kann","kannst","können","konnte"],"answer":0},{"type":"mcq","prompt":"Er ___ jeden Tag früh aufstehen.","options":["müssen","musst","muss","müsst"],"answer":2},{"type":"fill","prompt":"Du ___ hier nicht parken. (dürfen)","answer":"darfst","explain_tr":"du darfst."},{"type":"fill","prompt":"Wir ___ heute Abend ins Kino gehen. (wollen)","answer":"wollen","explain_tr":"wir wollen."},{"type":"mcq","prompt":"Welcher Satz ist richtig?","options":["Ich kann Deutsch sprechen.","Ich kann sprechen Deutsch.","Ich Deutsch kann sprechen.","Ich kann spreche Deutsch."],"answer":0,"explain_tr":"Ana fiil mastar olarak cümle sonuna gider."}]'::jsonb, 5) on conflict (language_code, slug) do update set title_tr = excluded.title_tr, title_target = excluded.title_target, cefr_level = excluded.cefr_level, summary_tr = excluded.summary_tr, examples = excluded.examples, practice_items = excluded.practice_items, order_index = excluded.order_index;
haben/sein (şimdiki zamanda) + Partizip II (cümle sonunda)

• Çoğu fiil “haben” alır: Ich habe Pizza gegessen.
• Hareket ve durum değişikliği bildiren fiiller “sein” alır: Wir sind nach Berlin gefahren. Er ist früh aufgestanden.
• Düzenli: ge-…-t (machen → gemacht); düzensiz: ge-…-en (gehen → gegangen, essen → gegessen).
• Ayrılabilen fiillerde ge- ortaya girer: aufstehen → aufgestanden.', '[{"text":"Ich habe Pizza gegessen.","tr":"Pizza yedim.","highlight":"habe"},{"text":"Wir sind nach Berlin gefahren.","tr":"Berlin''e gittik.","highlight":"sind"},{"text":"Sie hat das Buch gelesen.","tr":"Kitabı okudu.","highlight":"hat"},{"text":"Er ist früh aufgestanden.","tr":"Erken kalktı.","highlight":"ist"}]'::jsonb, '[{"type":"mcq","prompt":"Gestern ___ ich ins Kino gegangen.","options":["habe","bin","hat","ist"],"answer":1,"explain_tr":"gehen hareket fiilidir: sein alır."},{"type":"mcq","prompt":"Wir ___ Fußball gespielt.","options":["sind","haben","hat","bin"],"answer":1},{"type":"fill","prompt":"Sie ___ gestern einen Kuchen gebacken. (haben)","answer":"hat"},{"type":"fill","prompt":"Ich habe gestern Tee ___. (trinken)","answer":"getrunken"},{"type":"mcq","prompt":"Welches Partizip ist richtig? (fahren)","options":["gefahrt","gefahren","gefährt","gefahrnen"],"answer":1}]'::jsonb, 6) on conflict (language_code, slug) do update set title_tr = excluded.title_tr, title_target = excluded.title_target, cefr_level = excluded.cefr_level, summary_tr = excluded.summary_tr, examples = excluded.examples, practice_items = excluded.practice_items, order_index = excluded.order_index;
• Düz cümlede fiil 2. sıraya gider, ön ek CÜMLENİN SONUNDA kalır: Ich stehe um sieben Uhr auf.
• Modal fiille mastar birlikte kalır: Ich muss früh aufstehen.
• Perfekt’te ge- ön ekle fiil arasına girer: aufgestanden, eingekauft, angerufen.
• Ön ek vurgu alır: ÁUFstehen.', '[{"text":"Ich stehe um sieben Uhr auf.","tr":"Saat yedide kalkıyorum.","highlight":"stehe"},{"text":"Kommst du mit?","tr":"Sen de geliyor musun?","highlight":"Kommst"},{"text":"Ruf mich bitte an!","tr":"Lütfen beni ara!","highlight":"Ruf"},{"text":"Wir kaufen im Supermarkt ein.","tr":"Süpermarkette alışveriş yapıyoruz.","highlight":"kaufen"}]'::jsonb, '[{"type":"mcq","prompt":"Welcher Satz ist richtig?","options":["Ich aufstehe um 7 Uhr.","Ich stehe um 7 Uhr auf.","Um 7 Uhr ich stehe auf.","Ich stehe auf um 7 Uhr auf."],"answer":1},{"type":"mcq","prompt":"Er ___ seine Eltern jeden Sonntag ___.","options":["ruft … an","anruft … –","ruft … um","ruft … ein"],"answer":0,"explain_tr":"Fiil 2. sırada, ön ek sonda: Er ruft … an."},{"type":"fill","prompt":"Ich ___ dich morgen an. (anrufen)","answer":"rufe","explain_tr":"Fiil 2. sırada, “an” cümle sonunda."},{"type":"fill","prompt":"Der Film ___ um 20 Uhr an. (anfangen: er …)","answer":"fängt","explain_tr":"anfangen → er fängt an."},{"type":"mcq","prompt":"Ich muss morgen früh ___.","options":["aufstehen","stehe auf","auf stehen","aufgestehen"],"answer":0,"explain_tr":"Modal fiille mastar birlikte yazılır."}]'::jsonb, 7) on conflict (language_code, slug) do update set title_tr = excluded.title_tr, title_target = excluded.title_target, cefr_level = excluded.cefr_level, summary_tr = excluded.summary_tr, examples = excluded.examples, practice_items = excluded.practice_items, order_index = excluded.order_index;
• Artikel: der → dem, die → der, das → dem, çoğul die → den (+ isme -n: den Kindern).
• Zamirler: mir, dir, ihm (er), ihr (sie), ihm (es), uns, euch, ihnen.
• Her zaman Dativ isteyen edatlar: mit, nach, bei, seit, von, zu, aus (gegenüber): mit dem Bus, bei meiner Tante.
• Dativ isteyen fiiller: helfen, gehören, gefallen, danken: Das Buch gehört mir. Wie gefällt dir die Stadt?', '[{"text":"Ich gebe dem Kind einen Apfel.","tr":"Çocuğa bir elma veriyorum.","highlight":"dem Kind"},{"text":"Wir fahren mit dem Bus.","tr":"Otobüsle gidiyoruz.","highlight":"mit dem Bus"},{"text":"Das Buch gehört mir.","tr":"Kitap bana ait.","highlight":"mir"},{"text":"Ich wohne bei meiner Tante.","tr":"Teyzemin yanında oturuyorum.","highlight":"bei meiner Tante"}]'::jsonb, '[{"type":"mcq","prompt":"Ich fahre mit ___ Zug.","options":["der","dem","den","das"],"answer":1,"explain_tr":"“mit” her zaman Dativ ister; der Zug → dem Zug."},{"type":"mcq","prompt":"Sie hilft ___ Kind.","options":["das","dem","den","der"],"answer":1,"explain_tr":"helfen + Dativ."},{"type":"fill","prompt":"Das Auto gehört ___. (ich)","answer":"mir","explain_tr":"gehören + Dativ: mir."},{"type":"fill","prompt":"Wie geht es ___? (du)","answer":"dir","explain_tr":"Dativ zamiri: dir."},{"type":"mcq","prompt":"Wir kommen aus ___ Türkei.","options":["die","der","dem","den"],"answer":1,"explain_tr":"aus + Dativ; die Türkei → der Türkei."}]'::jsonb, 8) on conflict (language_code, slug) do update set title_tr = excluded.title_tr, title_target = excluded.title_target, cefr_level = excluded.cefr_level, summary_tr = excluded.summary_tr, examples = excluded.examples, practice_items = excluded.practice_items, order_index = excluded.order_index;
• Wo? (nerede?, durum) → Dativ: Das Buch liegt auf dem Tisch. Ich bin in der Küche.
• Wohin? (nereye?, hareket) → Akkusativ: Ich lege das Buch auf den Tisch. Ich gehe in die Küche.
• Konum fiilleri (stehen, liegen, sitzen, hängen) → Dativ; hareket fiilleri (stellen, legen, setzen, gehen) → Akkusativ.
• Kısaltmalar: in dem → im, an dem → am, in das → ins.', '[{"text":"Die Katze sitzt auf dem Sofa.","tr":"Kedi kanepede oturuyor.","highlight":"auf dem Sofa"},{"text":"Ich lege das Buch auf den Tisch.","tr":"Kitabı masanın üstüne koyuyorum.","highlight":"auf den Tisch"},{"text":"Wir sind im Park.","tr":"Parktayız.","highlight":"im Park"},{"text":"Er geht in die Schule.","tr":"Okula gidiyor.","highlight":"in die Schule"}]'::jsonb, '[{"type":"mcq","prompt":"Ich gehe in ___ Küche.","options":["die","der","dem","den"],"answer":0,"explain_tr":"Wohin? → Akkusativ: die Küche."},{"type":"mcq","prompt":"Der Hund liegt unter ___ Tisch.","options":["den","dem","der","das"],"answer":1,"explain_tr":"Wo? → Dativ: dem Tisch."},{"type":"fill","prompt":"Wohin stellst du die Flasche? Auf ___ Tisch. (den/dem)","answer":"den","explain_tr":"Wohin? → Akkusativ: den Tisch."},{"type":"fill","prompt":"Wo ist die Katze? Auf ___ Sofa. (das/dem)","answer":"dem","explain_tr":"Wo? → Dativ: dem Sofa."},{"type":"mcq","prompt":"Das Bild hängt an ___ Wand.","options":["die","der","dem","den"],"answer":1,"explain_tr":"Wo? → Dativ; die Wand → der Wand."}]'::jsonb, 9) on conflict (language_code, slug) do update set title_tr = excluded.title_tr, title_target = excluded.title_target, cefr_level = excluded.cefr_level, summary_tr = excluded.summary_tr, examples = excluded.examples, practice_items = excluded.practice_items, order_index = excluded.order_index;
• sein: ich war, du warst, er war, wir waren, ihr wart, sie waren
• haben: ich hatte, du hattest, er hatte, wir hatten …
• Modaller (umlaut düşer, -te eki): können → konnte, müssen → musste, wollen → wollte, dürfen → durfte, sollen → sollte.
Gestern war ich krank. Ich hatte Fieber. Ich konnte nicht arbeiten.', '[{"text":"Gestern war ich im Kino.","tr":"Dün sinemadaydım.","highlight":"war"},{"text":"Wir hatten keine Zeit.","tr":"Zamanımız yoktu.","highlight":"hatten"},{"text":"Er konnte nicht kommen.","tr":"Gelemedi.","highlight":"konnte"},{"text":"Als Kind wollte ich Pilot werden.","tr":"Çocukken pilot olmak istiyordum.","highlight":"wollte"}]'::jsonb, '[{"type":"mcq","prompt":"Letzten Sommer ___ wir in Wien.","options":["waren","sind","war","wart"],"answer":0},{"type":"mcq","prompt":"Als Kind ___ ich nicht schwimmen.","options":["kann","könnte","konnte","gekonnt"],"answer":2},{"type":"fill","prompt":"Gestern ___ ich sehr müde. (sein)","answer":"war","explain_tr":"ich war."},{"type":"fill","prompt":"Sie ___ keine Zeit. (haben – Präteritum)","answer":"hatte","explain_tr":"sie hatte."},{"type":"fill","prompt":"Er ___ gestern arbeiten. (müssen – Präteritum)","answer":"musste","explain_tr":"müssen → musste (umlaut düşer)."}]'::jsonb, 10) on conflict (language_code, slug) do update set title_tr = excluded.title_tr, title_target = excluded.title_target, cefr_level = excluded.cefr_level, summary_tr = excluded.summary_tr, examples = excluded.examples, practice_items = excluded.practice_items, order_index = excluded.order_index;
• Belirli artikelden sonra (der/die/das): Nom.: -e (der gute Mann, die gute Frau, das gute Kind). Akk.: m → -en (den guten Mann), f/n → -e. Dativ ve çoğul: -en (mit dem guten Mann, die guten Kinder).
• Belirsiz artikelden sonra (ein/eine): Nom. m → -er (ein guter Mann), n → -es (ein gutes Kind), f → -e (eine gute Frau). Akk. m → -en (einen guten Mann). Dativ: -en (mit einem guten Freund).
• Yüklemde (ist) sıfat çekimlenmez: Der Mann ist gut.', '[{"text":"Der kleine Hund schläft.","tr":"Küçük köpek uyuyor.","highlight":"kleine"},{"text":"Ich kaufe den roten Mantel.","tr":"Kırmızı montu alıyorum.","highlight":"roten"},{"text":"Das ist ein neues Auto.","tr":"Bu yeni bir araba.","highlight":"neues"},{"text":"Wir wohnen in einem großen Haus.","tr":"Büyük bir evde oturuyoruz.","highlight":"großen"}]'::jsonb, '[{"type":"mcq","prompt":"Das ist eine ___ Idee.","options":["gute","guter","gutes","guten"],"answer":0,"explain_tr":"eine Idee (f, Nom.) → eine gute Idee."},{"type":"mcq","prompt":"Ich sehe den ___ Mann.","options":["alte","alter","alten","altes"],"answer":2,"explain_tr":"Akk. m: den alten Mann."},{"type":"fill","prompt":"Das ist ein ___ Buch. (interessant)","answer":"interessantes","explain_tr":"ein Buch (n, Nom.) → -es."},{"type":"fill","prompt":"Sie trägt ein ___ Kleid. (blau)","answer":"blaues","explain_tr":"ein Kleid (n, Akk.) → -es."},{"type":"mcq","prompt":"Mit dem ___ Kind spiele ich gern.","options":["kleine","kleiner","kleinen","kleines"],"answer":2,"explain_tr":"Dativ → -en."}]'::jsonb, 11) on conflict (language_code, slug) do update set title_tr = excluded.title_tr, title_target = excluded.title_target, cefr_level = excluded.cefr_level, summary_tr = excluded.summary_tr, examples = excluded.examples, practice_items = excluded.practice_items, order_index = excluded.order_index;
• als → geçmişte TEK SEFER olan olay veya uzun bir dönem: Als ich ein Kind war, wohnte ich in Ankara. Als ich nach Hause kam, war niemand da.
• wenn → şimdiki zaman/gelecek ve geçmişte TEKRARLANAN olaylar: Wenn es regnet, bleibe ich zu Hause. Immer wenn ich Zeit hatte, ging ich spazieren.
• wenn aynı zamanda koşul bildirir (“eğer”): Wenn du willst, helfe ich dir.
• İkisinde de çekimli fiil yan cümlenin SONUNA gider.', '[{"text":"Als ich ein Kind war, spielte ich viel draußen.","tr":"Çocukken çok dışarıda oynardım.","highlight":"Als ich ein Kind war"},{"text":"Wenn es regnet, bleibe ich zu Hause.","tr":"Yağmur yağarsa evde kalırım.","highlight":"Wenn es regnet"},{"text":"Immer wenn ich Zeit hatte, ging ich spazieren.","tr":"Ne zaman vaktim olsa yürüyüşe çıkardım.","highlight":"wenn ich Zeit hatte"},{"text":"Als wir ankamen, war es schon dunkel.","tr":"Vardığımızda hava zaten kararmıştı.","highlight":"Als wir ankamen"}]'::jsonb, '[{"type":"mcq","prompt":"___ ich gestern nach Hause kam, war niemand da.","options":["Wenn","Als","Wann","Falls"],"answer":1,"explain_tr":"Geçmişte tek sefer → als."},{"type":"mcq","prompt":"___ du Hilfe brauchst, ruf mich an.","options":["Als","Wenn","Wann","Weil"],"answer":1},{"type":"fill","prompt":"___ ich zehn Jahre alt war, zog ich nach Berlin. (wenn/als)","answer":"als","explain_tr":"Geçmişte tek bir dönem/olay → als."},{"type":"fill","prompt":"Immer ___ ich Kopfschmerzen habe, trinke ich Tee. (wenn/als)","answer":"wenn","explain_tr":"Tekrarlanan olay → wenn."},{"type":"mcq","prompt":"Welcher Satz ist richtig?","options":["Wenn ich müde bin, gehe ich früh ins Bett.","Wenn ich bin müde, gehe ich früh ins Bett.","Wenn ich müde bin, ich gehe früh ins Bett.","Als ich müde bin, gehe ich früh ins Bett."],"answer":0}]'::jsonb, 12) on conflict (language_code, slug) do update set title_tr = excluded.title_tr, title_target = excluded.title_target, cefr_level = excluded.cefr_level, summary_tr = excluded.summary_tr, examples = excluded.examples, practice_items = excluded.practice_items, order_index = excluded.order_index;

Ich bleibe zu Hause, weil ich krank bin.
Er sagt, dass er müde ist.

Perfekt’te çekimli yardımcı fiil en sondadır: …, weil er schlecht geschlafen hat.
Modal fiilli cümlede: …, weil ich in Berlin arbeiten möchte.

Yan cümle önce gelirse ana cümlede fiil hemen başa geçer: Weil ich krank bin, bleibe ich zu Hause.', '[{"text":"Ich bleibe zu Hause, weil ich krank bin.","tr":"Hasta olduğum için evde kalıyorum.","highlight":"weil ich krank bin"},{"text":"Sie sagt, dass das Wetter schön ist.","tr":"Havanın güzel olduğunu söylüyor.","highlight":"dass das Wetter schön ist"},{"text":"Ich weiß, dass du Zeit hast.","tr":"Zamanın olduğunu biliyorum.","highlight":"dass du Zeit hast"},{"text":"Er ist müde, weil er schlecht geschlafen hat.","tr":"Kötü uyuduğu için yorgun.","highlight":"weil er schlecht geschlafen hat"}]'::jsonb, '[{"type":"mcq","prompt":"Ich komme nicht, weil ich ___.","options":["bin krank","krank bin","krank sein","ist krank"],"answer":1},{"type":"mcq","prompt":"Ich glaube, dass er morgen ___.","options":["kommt","kommen","er kommt","kommst"],"answer":0},{"type":"fill","prompt":"Ich lerne Deutsch, weil ich in Berlin ___ möchte. (arbeiten)","answer":"arbeiten"},{"type":"mcq","prompt":"Sie ist müde, weil sie wenig ___.","options":["geschlafen hat","hat geschlafen","geschlafen","schläft hat"],"answer":0},{"type":"fill","prompt":"Ich weiß, dass du heute viel Arbeit ___. (haben)","answer":"hast"}]'::jsonb, 13) on conflict (language_code, slug) do update set title_tr = excluded.title_tr, title_target = excluded.title_target, cefr_level = excluded.cefr_level, summary_tr = excluded.summary_tr, examples = excluded.examples, practice_items = excluded.practice_items, order_index = excluded.order_index;
• Cinsiyet ve sayı: bağlandığı isme göre; hâl: relativ cümledeki göreve göre.
• Nom.: der / die / das / die · Akk.: den / die / das / die · Dativ: dem / der / dem / denen
Der Mann, der dort steht, ist mein Lehrer.
Das ist der Film, den ich gestern gesehen habe.
Die Kinder, denen ich helfe, sind nett.', '[{"text":"Der Mann, der dort steht, ist mein Lehrer.","tr":"Orada duran adam benim öğretmenim.","highlight":"der dort steht"},{"text":"Das Buch, das ich lese, ist spannend.","tr":"Okuduğum kitap heyecan verici.","highlight":"das ich lese"},{"text":"Das ist der Film, den ich gesehen habe.","tr":"Bu, izlediğim film.","highlight":"den ich gesehen habe"},{"text":"Die Kinder, denen ich helfe, sind nett.","tr":"Yardım ettiğim çocuklar tatlı.","highlight":"denen ich helfe"}]'::jsonb, '[{"type":"mcq","prompt":"Das ist die Frau, ___ im Büro arbeitet.","options":["der","die","den","das"],"answer":1,"explain_tr":"Özne olarak Nominativ: die."},{"type":"mcq","prompt":"Das ist der Mann, ___ ich gestern gesehen habe.","options":["der","dem","den","dessen"],"answer":2,"explain_tr":"Nesne (Akkusativ), maskulin: den."},{"type":"fill","prompt":"Das Auto, ___ dort steht, gehört mir. (der/die/das)","answer":"das","explain_tr":"das Auto → das."},{"type":"fill","prompt":"Wo ist das Buch, ___ ich gestern gekauft habe? (der/die/das)","answer":"das","explain_tr":"Nesne, nötr: das."},{"type":"mcq","prompt":"Die Kinder, ___ ich helfe, sind nett.","options":["die","den","denen","der"],"answer":2,"explain_tr":"helfen + Dativ, çoğul: denen."}]'::jsonb, 14) on conflict (language_code, slug) do update set title_tr = excluded.title_tr, title_target = excluded.title_target, cefr_level = excluded.cefr_level, summary_tr = excluded.summary_tr, examples = excluded.examples, practice_items = excluded.practice_items, order_index = excluded.order_index;
• Akkusativ: ich freue mich · du freust dich · er/sie/es freut sich · wir freuen uns · ihr freut euch · sie freuen sich
• Dativ (başka bir tümleç varsa): Ich wasche mir die Hände. Ich kaufe mir ein Auto. (mir, dir, sich, uns, euch, sich)
• Bazı fiiller sabit edatla kullanılır: sich freuen auf (+Akk.), sich interessieren für (+Akk.), sich ärgern über (+Akk.).', '[{"text":"Ich freue mich auf den Urlaub.","tr":"Tatili dört gözle bekliyorum.","highlight":"freue mich"},{"text":"Wir treffen uns um acht Uhr.","tr":"Saat sekizde buluşuyoruz.","highlight":"treffen uns"},{"text":"Er interessiert sich für Musik.","tr":"Müzikle ilgileniyor.","highlight":"interessiert sich"},{"text":"Ich wasche mir die Hände.","tr":"Ellerimi yıkıyorum.","highlight":"wasche mir"}]'::jsonb, '[{"type":"mcq","prompt":"Sie setzt ___ auf den Stuhl.","options":["mich","dich","sich","uns"],"answer":2},{"type":"mcq","prompt":"Ich wasche ___ die Hände.","options":["mich","mir","sich","uns"],"answer":1,"explain_tr":"Başka bir tümleç (die Hände) olduğunda Dativ: mir."},{"type":"fill","prompt":"Wir treffen ___ morgen. (wir)","answer":"uns","explain_tr":"wir → uns."},{"type":"fill","prompt":"Er freut ___ auf das Wochenende.","answer":"sich","explain_tr":"er → sich."},{"type":"mcq","prompt":"Du interessierst ___ für Fußball.","options":["mich","dich","sich","dir"],"answer":1}]'::jsonb, 15) on conflict (language_code, slug) do update set title_tr = excluded.title_tr, title_target = excluded.title_target, cefr_level = excluded.cefr_level, summary_tr = excluded.summary_tr, examples = excluded.examples, practice_items = excluded.practice_items, order_index = excluded.order_index;
• Präsens: Das Haus wird gebaut. Die Hausaufgaben werden gemacht.
• Präteritum: Das Haus wurde 1990 gebaut.
• Yapan belirtilirse von + Dativ: Das Buch wird von dem Lehrer gelesen.
• Modal fiille: Das Problem muss gelöst werden.
Aktif → Pasif: Man repariert das Auto. → Das Auto wird repariert.', '[{"text":"Das Auto wird repariert.","tr":"Araba tamir ediliyor.","highlight":"wird repariert"},{"text":"Hier werden Brötchen gebacken.","tr":"Burada çörek pişirilir.","highlight":"werden Brötchen gebacken"},{"text":"Das Haus wurde 1990 gebaut.","tr":"Ev 1990’da yapıldı.","highlight":"wurde 1990 gebaut"},{"text":"Das Buch wird von vielen Menschen gelesen.","tr":"Kitap birçok insan tarafından okunuyor.","highlight":"wird von vielen Menschen gelesen"}]'::jsonb, '[{"type":"mcq","prompt":"Der Kuchen ___ von meiner Mutter gebacken.","options":["wird","werden","wurden","ist"],"answer":0},{"type":"mcq","prompt":"Die Hausaufgaben ___ jeden Tag gemacht.","options":["wird","werden","wurde","sind"],"answer":1,"explain_tr":"Çoğul özne: werden."},{"type":"fill","prompt":"Das Haus ___ im Jahr 1900 gebaut. (werden – Präteritum)","answer":"wurde","explain_tr":"werden → wurde."},{"type":"fill","prompt":"Die Tür wird von dem Mann ___. (öffnen – Partizip II)","answer":"geöffnet","explain_tr":"öffnen → geöffnet."},{"type":"mcq","prompt":"Welcher Satz ist Passiv?","options":["Ich repariere das Auto.","Das Auto wird repariert.","Das Auto repariert mich.","Ich habe das Auto repariert."],"answer":1}]'::jsonb, 16) on conflict (language_code, slug) do update set title_tr = excluded.title_tr, title_target = excluded.title_target, cefr_level = excluded.cefr_level, summary_tr = excluded.summary_tr, examples = excluded.examples, practice_items = excluded.practice_items, order_index = excluded.order_index;
• würde + mastar: Ich würde gern nach Italien fahren.
• Sık kullanılan fiillerde özel biçimler: sein → wäre, haben → hätte, können → könnte, müssen → müsste, wissen → wüsste.
• Gerçek dışı koşul: Wenn ich reich wäre, würde ich ein Haus kaufen. Wenn ich Zeit hätte, käme ich.
• Kibar rica: Könnten Sie mir helfen? Hätten Sie einen Moment Zeit?
• Tavsiye: An deiner Stelle würde ich zum Arzt gehen.', '[{"text":"Wenn ich reich wäre, würde ich reisen.","tr":"Zengin olsam seyahat ederdim.","highlight":"wäre"},{"text":"Wenn ich Zeit hätte, würde ich öfter kommen.","tr":"Zamanım olsa daha sık gelirdim.","highlight":"hätte"},{"text":"Könnten Sie mir bitte helfen?","tr":"Bana yardım edebilir misiniz lütfen?","highlight":"Könnten"},{"text":"An deiner Stelle würde ich nicht warten.","tr":"Senin yerinde olsam beklemezdim.","highlight":"würde ich nicht warten"}]'::jsonb, '[{"type":"mcq","prompt":"Wenn ich reich ___, würde ich ein Haus kaufen.","options":["bin","wäre","war","würde sein"],"answer":1},{"type":"mcq","prompt":"An deiner Stelle ___ ich zum Arzt gehen.","options":["werde","würde","wurde","wäre"],"answer":1},{"type":"fill","prompt":"Wenn ich mehr Zeit ___, würde ich öfter kommen. (haben – Konjunktiv II)","answer":"hätte","explain_tr":"haben → hätte."},{"type":"fill","prompt":"___ Sie mir bitte helfen? (können – Konjunktiv II)","answer":"Könnten","explain_tr":"Kibar rica: Könnten Sie…?"},{"type":"mcq","prompt":"Ich ___ gern ein Eis essen.","options":["würde","wurde","werde","würden"],"answer":0}]'::jsonb, 17) on conflict (language_code, slug) do update set title_tr = excluded.title_tr, title_target = excluded.title_target, cefr_level = excluded.cefr_level, summary_tr = excluded.summary_tr, examples = excluded.examples, practice_items = excluded.practice_items, order_index = excluded.order_index;
• je … desto/umso + karşılaştırma: Je mehr du übst, desto besser wirst du.
• nicht nur … sondern auch: Sie spricht nicht nur Englisch, sondern auch Spanisch.
• sowohl … als auch: Er ist sowohl intelligent als auch fleißig.
• weder … noch (ikisi de değil): Ich möchte weder Tee noch Kaffee.
• entweder … oder: Wir fahren entweder nach Wien oder nach Prag.
• “je” cümlesinde fiil sonda, “desto” cümlesinde fiil 2. sıradadır.', '[{"text":"Je mehr du übst, desto besser wirst du.","tr":"Ne kadar çok çalışırsan o kadar iyi olursun.","highlight":"Je mehr du übst, desto besser"},{"text":"Sie spricht nicht nur Englisch, sondern auch Spanisch.","tr":"Yalnızca İngilizce değil, İspanyolca da konuşuyor.","highlight":"nicht nur Englisch, sondern auch Spanisch"},{"text":"Ich möchte weder Tee noch Kaffee.","tr":"Ne çay ne de kahve istiyorum.","highlight":"weder Tee noch Kaffee"},{"text":"Wir fahren entweder nach Wien oder nach Prag.","tr":"Ya Viyana’ya ya da Prag’a gidiyoruz.","highlight":"entweder nach Wien oder nach Prag"}]'::jsonb, '[{"type":"mcq","prompt":"___ mehr ich lerne, desto besser verstehe ich.","options":["Je","Wenn","Umso","Weil"],"answer":0,"explain_tr":"je + karşılaştırma … desto + karşılaştırma."},{"type":"mcq","prompt":"Er ist sowohl intelligent ___ fleißig.","options":["oder","als auch","noch","sondern"],"answer":1},{"type":"fill","prompt":"Sie hat weder Zeit ___ Lust. (noch/oder)","answer":"noch","explain_tr":"weder … noch"},{"type":"fill","prompt":"Nicht nur der Chef, ___ auch die Kollegen waren begeistert. (sondern/aber)","answer":"sondern","explain_tr":"nicht nur … sondern auch"},{"type":"mcq","prompt":"Welcher Satz ist richtig?","options":["Entweder bleibe ich hier oder ich gehe nach Hause.","Entweder bleibe ich hier noch ich gehe nach Hause.","Weder bleibe ich hier oder ich gehe nach Hause.","Entweder bleibe ich hier sondern ich gehe nach Hause."],"answer":0}]'::jsonb, 18) on conflict (language_code, slug) do update set title_tr = excluded.title_tr, title_target = excluded.title_target, cefr_level = excluded.cefr_level, summary_tr = excluded.summary_tr, examples = excluded.examples, practice_items = excluded.practice_items, order_index = excluded.order_index;
• Oluşum: mastar kökü + -e, -est, -e, -en, -et, -en → er komme, sie habe, er fahre.
• sein: er sei, sie seien (ich sei, du seiest).
• Konjunktiv I biçimi Indikativ ile aynıysa Konjunktiv II kullanılır: sie haben → sie hätten; sie kommen → sie kämen/würden kommen.
Er sagt: „Ich bin müde.“ → Er sagt, er sei müde.
Sie sagte: „Ich habe keine Zeit.“ → Sie sagte, sie habe keine Zeit.', '[{"text":"Er sagt, er sei müde.","tr":"Yorgun olduğunu söylüyor.","highlight":"sei"},{"text":"Sie sagte, sie habe keine Zeit.","tr":"Zamanı olmadığını söyledi.","highlight":"habe"},{"text":"Der Politiker sagte, er fahre morgen nach Paris.","tr":"Siyasetçi yarın Paris’e gideceğini söyledi.","highlight":"fahre"},{"text":"Sie sagten, sie hätten keine Zeit.","tr":"Zamanları olmadığını söylediler.","highlight":"hätten"}]'::jsonb, '[{"type":"mcq","prompt":"Er sagt, er ___ krank. (Konjunktiv I)","options":["ist","sei","war","sein"],"answer":1},{"type":"mcq","prompt":"Sie sagten, sie ___ keine Zeit. (haben; K I = Indikativ)","options":["haben","hätten","habe","hatten"],"answer":1,"explain_tr":"sie haben = Indikativ ile aynı, bu yüzden Konjunktiv II: hätten."},{"type":"fill","prompt":"Sie sagt, sie ___ Hunger. (haben, Konjunktiv I)","answer":"habe","explain_tr":"sie habe."},{"type":"fill","prompt":"Er sagte, er ___ morgen nach Berlin. (fahren, Konjunktiv I)","answer":"fahre","explain_tr":"er fahre."},{"type":"mcq","prompt":"Er sagte, er ___ gestern im Kino gewesen. (Konjunktiv I)","options":["ist","sei","war","sein"],"answer":1}]'::jsonb, 19) on conflict (language_code, slug) do update set title_tr = excluded.title_tr, title_target = excluded.title_target, cefr_level = excluded.cefr_level, summary_tr = excluded.summary_tr, examples = excluded.examples, practice_items = excluded.practice_items, order_index = excluded.order_index;
• Artikel: der → des, die → der, das → des, çoğul die → der.
• Maskulin ve nötr isimler -s veya -es alır: des Mannes, des Kindes, des Hauses.
• Genitiv isteyen edatlar: wegen, trotz, während, statt/anstatt, innerhalb, außerhalb.
Wegen des Wetters bleiben wir zu Hause.
Trotz der Kälte gehen wir spazieren.
Konuşmada çoğu zaman Dativ de kullanılır (wegen dem Wetter), yazıda Genitiv doğrudur.', '[{"text":"Das ist das Auto meines Vaters.","tr":"Bu babamın arabası.","highlight":"meines Vaters"},{"text":"Wegen des Wetters bleiben wir zu Hause.","tr":"Hava yüzünden evde kalıyoruz.","highlight":"Wegen des Wetters"},{"text":"Trotz der Kälte gehen wir spazieren.","tr":"Soğuğa rağmen yürüyüşe çıkıyoruz.","highlight":"Trotz der Kälte"},{"text":"Während des Sommers ist es heiß.","tr":"Yaz boyunca hava sıcak.","highlight":"Während des Sommers"}]'::jsonb, '[{"type":"mcq","prompt":"Das ist das Fahrrad ___ Lehrers.","options":["der","des","dem","den"],"answer":1},{"type":"mcq","prompt":"Trotz ___ Krankheit arbeitet sie.","options":["die","der","des","dem"],"answer":1,"explain_tr":"die Krankheit (f) → der Krankheit."},{"type":"fill","prompt":"Wegen ___ Regens bleiben wir zu Hause. (der/des)","answer":"des","explain_tr":"der Regen (m) → des Regens."},{"type":"fill","prompt":"Während ___ Urlaubs habe ich viel gelesen. (der/des)","answer":"des","explain_tr":"der Urlaub (m) → des Urlaubs."},{"type":"mcq","prompt":"Die Tasche ___ Frau liegt hier.","options":["des","der","dem","den"],"answer":1}]'::jsonb, 20) on conflict (language_code, slug) do update set title_tr = excluded.title_tr, title_target = excluded.title_target, cefr_level = excluded.cefr_level, summary_tr = excluded.summary_tr, examples = excluded.examples, practice_items = excluded.practice_items, order_index = excluded.order_index;
• haben fiilleri: hätte + Partizip II → Ich hätte gelernt.
• sein ve hareket fiilleri: wäre + Partizip II → Ich wäre gekommen.
• Koşul: Wenn ich das gewusst hätte, wäre ich gekommen.
• Wenn’siz koşul: Hätte ich das gewusst, wäre ich gekommen.
• Modallerle: Ich hätte kommen können.', '[{"text":"Wenn ich das gewusst hätte, wäre ich gekommen.","tr":"Bunu bilseydim gelirdim.","highlight":"gewusst hätte"},{"text":"Ich wäre gern mitgekommen.","tr":"Memnuniyetle gelirdim.","highlight":"wäre"},{"text":"Wenn sie mehr gelernt hätte, hätte sie die Prüfung bestanden.","tr":"Daha çok çalışsaydı sınavı geçerdi.","highlight":"hätte sie die Prüfung bestanden"},{"text":"Hätte ich mehr Zeit gehabt, wäre ich geblieben.","tr":"Daha çok zamanım olsaydı kalırdım.","highlight":"Hätte ich mehr Zeit gehabt"}]'::jsonb, '[{"type":"mcq","prompt":"Wenn ich Zeit gehabt ___, wäre ich gekommen.","options":["hätte","wäre","hatte","würde"],"answer":0},{"type":"mcq","prompt":"Wenn wir das gewusst ___, hätten wir euch angerufen.","options":["hatten","hätten","haben","wären"],"answer":1},{"type":"fill","prompt":"Ich ___ gern mitgekommen, aber ich war krank. (sein – Konjunktiv II)","answer":"wäre","explain_tr":"kommen hareket fiili → wäre gekommen."},{"type":"fill","prompt":"Wenn sie mehr gelernt hätte, ___ sie die Prüfung bestanden. (haben – Konjunktiv II)","answer":"hätte","explain_tr":"Ana cümle: hätte sie … bestanden."},{"type":"mcq","prompt":"Welcher Satz ist richtig?","options":["Wenn ich das wüsste, wäre ich gekommen.","Wenn ich das gewusst hätte, wäre ich gekommen.","Wenn ich das gewusst habe, wäre ich gekommen.","Wenn ich das gewusst hätte, würde ich gekommen."],"answer":1}]'::jsonb, 21) on conflict (language_code, slug) do update set title_tr = excluded.title_tr, title_target = excluded.title_target, cefr_level = excluded.cefr_level, summary_tr = excluded.summary_tr, examples = excluded.examples, practice_items = excluded.practice_items, order_index = excluded.order_index;
• Fiil → isim: untersuchen → die Untersuchung · entscheiden → die Entscheidung · fahren → die Fahrt · lesen → das Lesen (mastar isim).
• Sıfat → isim: schwierig → die Schwierigkeit · frei → die Freiheit.
• Yan cümle → edat + isim (Genitiv): Weil es stark regnet … → Wegen des starken Regens … · Obwohl es kalt war … → Trotz der Kälte … · Nachdem er angekommen war … → Nach seiner Ankunft …
• Nominalstil kısa ve ağırdır; konuşmada yan cümle (Verbalstil) tercih edilir.', '[{"text":"Wegen des starken Regens fällt das Fest aus.","tr":"Şiddetli yağmur nedeniyle şenlik iptal oluyor.","highlight":"Wegen des starken Regens"},{"text":"Nach der Untersuchung wurde ein Medikament verschrieben.","tr":"Muayeneden sonra bir ilaç yazıldı.","highlight":"Nach der Untersuchung"},{"text":"Das Lesen von Fachtexten erfordert Konzentration.","tr":"Uzmanlık metinlerini okumak dikkat gerektirir.","highlight":"Das Lesen"},{"text":"Trotz der hohen Kosten entschied sich die Firma für das Projekt.","tr":"Yüksek maliyete rağmen şirket projeyi seçti.","highlight":"Trotz der hohen Kosten"}]'::jsonb, '[{"type":"mcq","prompt":"Weil er krank war, blieb er zu Hause. = ___ blieb er zu Hause.","options":["Wegen seiner Krankheit","Trotz seiner Krankheit","Statt seiner Krankheit","Ohne seine Krankheit"],"answer":0,"explain_tr":"weil → wegen + Genitiv."},{"type":"mcq","prompt":"Das Verb „entscheiden“ wird zum Nomen: die ___.","options":["Entscheidung","Entscheidnis","Entscheidheit","Entscheidt"],"answer":0},{"type":"fill","prompt":"Obwohl es kalt war, gingen wir spazieren. = ___ der Kälte gingen wir spazieren. (Trotz/Wegen)","answer":"Trotz","explain_tr":"obwohl → trotz + Genitiv."},{"type":"fill","prompt":"Das Verb „untersuchen“ → die ___. (-ung)","answer":"Untersuchung","explain_tr":"-ung ile fiilden isim türetilir."},{"type":"mcq","prompt":"Welcher Satz ist nominalisiert?","options":["Nachdem er angekommen war, rief er an.","Nach seiner Ankunft rief er an.","Als er ankam, rief er an.","Er rief an, weil er ankam."],"answer":1}]'::jsonb, 22) on conflict (language_code, slug) do update set title_tr = excluded.title_tr, title_target = excluded.title_target, cefr_level = excluded.cefr_level, summary_tr = excluded.summary_tr, examples = excluded.examples, practice_items = excluded.practice_items, order_index = excluded.order_index;
• Partizip I (mastar + d) → etken, eş zamanlı: der spielende Junge = der Junge, der spielt.
• Partizip II → edilgen/tamamlanmış: das gelöste Problem = das Problem, das gelöst wurde.
• Genişletilmiş: Ek bilgiler artikel ile partizip arasına girer: der im Garten spielende Junge · die von der Regierung beschlossenen Maßnahmen.
• Sonuç yazı dilinde yoğun ve kısadır; sıfat ekleri normal sıfat gibi eklenir (-e, -en, -er, -es).', '[{"text":"Der im Garten spielende Junge ist mein Neffe.","tr":"Bahçede oynayan çocuk benim yeğenim.","highlight":"im Garten spielende"},{"text":"Das gelöste Problem war nicht schwierig.","tr":"Çözülen sorun zor değildi.","highlight":"gelöste"},{"text":"Die von der Regierung beschlossenen Maßnahmen treten morgen in Kraft.","tr":"Hükümetin aldığı önlemler yarın yürürlüğe giriyor.","highlight":"von der Regierung beschlossenen"},{"text":"Wir lesen einen interessanten, kürzlich erschienenen Artikel.","tr":"Yakın zamanda yayımlanmış ilginç bir makale okuyoruz.","highlight":"kürzlich erschienenen"}]'::jsonb, '[{"type":"mcq","prompt":"Der Junge, der im Garten spielt = der im Garten ___ Junge","options":["spielende","gespielte","spielte","spielenden"],"answer":0,"explain_tr":"Etken ve eş zamanlı: Partizip I + sıfat eki."},{"type":"mcq","prompt":"Das Problem, das gelöst wurde = das ___ Problem","options":["lösende","gelöste","gelöst","lösenden"],"answer":1,"explain_tr":"Edilgen: Partizip II + sıfat eki."},{"type":"fill","prompt":"Die Frau, die dort wartet = die dort ___ Frau (warten – Partizip I, ekli)","answer":"wartende","explain_tr":"warten + d + e = wartende"},{"type":"fill","prompt":"Das Auto, das gestohlen wurde = das ___ Auto (stehlen – Partizip II, ekli)","answer":"gestohlene","explain_tr":"gestohlen + e"},{"type":"mcq","prompt":"Welche Form ist richtig?","options":["das von mir gelesene Buch","das von mir lesende Buch","das von mir gelesen Buch","das von mir liest Buch"],"answer":0}]'::jsonb, 23) on conflict (language_code, slug) do update set title_tr = excluded.title_tr, title_target = excluded.title_target, cefr_level = excluded.cefr_level, summary_tr = excluded.summary_tr, examples = excluded.examples, practice_items = excluded.practice_items, order_index = excluded.order_index;
• indem → araç/yol (“-erek”): Du kannst dein Deutsch verbessern, indem du viel liest.
• sodass / so dass → sonuç: Es regnete stark, sodass das Spiel abgesagt wurde.
• sofern / falls → koşul: Sofern keine Probleme auftreten, beginnen wir am Montag.
• es sei denn (, dass) → istisna: Ich komme, es sei denn, ich muss arbeiten.
• Ayrılabilen fiiller yan cümlede birleşik yazılır: …, indem sie wenig ausging.', '[{"text":"Du kannst dein Deutsch verbessern, indem du viel liest.","tr":"Çok okuyarak Almancanı geliştirebilirsin.","highlight":"indem du viel liest"},{"text":"Es regnete stark, sodass das Spiel abgesagt wurde.","tr":"Çok yağmur yağdı, bu yüzden maç iptal edildi.","highlight":"sodass das Spiel abgesagt wurde"},{"text":"Ich komme, es sei denn, ich muss arbeiten.","tr":"Gelirim, çalışmam gerekmedikçe.","highlight":"es sei denn, ich muss arbeiten"},{"text":"Sofern keine Probleme auftreten, beginnen wir am Montag.","tr":"Sorun çıkmazsa Pazartesi başlıyoruz.","highlight":"Sofern keine Probleme auftreten"}]'::jsonb, '[{"type":"mcq","prompt":"Man lernt schwimmen, ___ man regelmäßig übt.","options":["indem","sodass","obwohl","damit"],"answer":0,"explain_tr":"Yol/araç: indem."},{"type":"mcq","prompt":"Er hat laut gesprochen, ___ alle ihn hören konnten.","options":["indem","sodass","falls","obwohl"],"answer":1,"explain_tr":"Sonuç: sodass."},{"type":"fill","prompt":"Wir bleiben zu Hause, es ___ denn, das Wetter wird besser. (sei/ist)","answer":"sei","explain_tr":"Sabit kalıp: es sei denn."},{"type":"fill","prompt":"___ keine Fragen mehr bestehen, beenden wir die Sitzung. (Sofern/Obwohl)","answer":"Sofern","explain_tr":"Koşul: sofern."},{"type":"mcq","prompt":"Welcher Satz ist richtig?","options":["Sie sparte Geld, indem sie wenig ausging.","Sie sparte Geld, indem sie ging wenig aus.","Sie sparte Geld, indem ging sie wenig aus.","Sie sparte Geld, indem wenig sie ausging."],"answer":0,"explain_tr":"Yan cümlede çekimli fiil sonda."}]'::jsonb, 24) on conflict (language_code, slug) do update set title_tr = excluded.title_tr, title_target = excluded.title_target, cefr_level = excluded.cefr_level, summary_tr = excluded.summary_tr, examples = excluded.examples, practice_items = excluded.practice_items, order_index = excluded.order_index;
